1
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:08,120
According to Nam Hee,
Seung Yong cried yesterday.

2
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:09,290
Why?

3
00:00:09,837 --> 00:00:12,737
He said that once it was over,
he realized how sorry he was.

4
00:00:12,737 --> 00:00:14,107
He hadn't fully understood
the situation until then.

5
00:00:14,907 --> 00:00:17,947
A lot of my teammates feel that...

6
00:00:18,407 --> 00:00:21,017
the best way to get back at them is...

7
00:00:21,347 --> 00:00:24,317
to win the Money Challenge
and eliminate them.

8
00:00:24,417 --> 00:00:28,157
That only made us more determined to win,

9
00:00:28,157 --> 00:00:31,257
and I want to lead our alliance
to victory.

10
00:00:33,457 --> 00:00:36,627
Keun Woo, this one is on you.

11
00:00:37,297 --> 00:00:39,237
Back in Season One,
you were amazing at finding things.

12
00:00:39,237 --> 00:00:40,297
You're the key player.

13
00:00:40,397 --> 00:00:42,037
- No, don't say that.
- Right.

14
00:00:42,237 --> 00:00:44,767
It's because I can handle my part,

15
00:00:44,767 --> 00:00:46,337
but the people going after me...

16
00:00:46,337 --> 00:00:48,137
- I need to do my part too.
- Keun Woo needs...

17
00:00:49,247 --> 00:00:50,307
to cover a lot of ground...

18
00:00:50,307 --> 00:00:53,117
and grab all the obvious targets quickly.

19
00:00:53,117 --> 00:00:55,347
You should search those
that are hard to find.

20
00:00:55,987 --> 00:00:58,487
We have to win this time
even if it's just out of frustration.

21
00:00:58,687 --> 00:01:00,717
Ji Min, we're winning this one
no matter what.

22
00:01:01,357 --> 00:01:02,427
I don't see us losing.

23
00:01:03,257 --> 00:01:05,757
Right? But Seung Yong seems to be
good with numbers.

24
00:01:07,257 --> 00:01:10,497
Honestly, I wasn't this fired up before.

25
00:01:10,997 --> 00:01:12,797
But now that Heist Day is over,

26
00:01:12,937 --> 00:01:14,697
we have to win this.

27
00:01:14,967 --> 00:01:18,437
I'm going to destroy those guys today.

28
00:01:18,637 --> 00:01:20,477
I'm getting my revenge for yesterday.

29
00:01:20,477 --> 00:01:22,477
We'll crush them during the game.

30
00:01:23,077 --> 00:01:25,347
Darn it. This works out
because I wanted to run.

31
00:01:26,347 --> 00:01:27,477
Let's survive no matter what.

32
00:01:27,477 --> 00:01:29,817
That sounds great. We're winning today.

33
00:01:31,547 --> 00:01:34,757
To be honest,
I was confident about today's game.

34
00:01:35,087 --> 00:01:36,387
We have Ji Hoo on our team.

35
00:01:36,687 --> 00:01:37,687
He's from KAIST.

36
00:01:38,357 --> 00:01:39,597
We're definitely winning.

37
00:01:39,927 --> 00:01:44,197
We have over
an 80-percent chance of winning.

38
00:01:44,927 --> 00:01:47,137
We have a very good chance
of winning this game.

39
00:01:47,737 --> 00:01:49,067
Right.

40
00:01:50,167 --> 00:01:52,807
As long as we find the equations
and solve them well.

41
00:01:54,577 --> 00:01:55,847
We have Ji Hoo with us.

42
00:01:56,047 --> 00:01:59,277
Ji Hoo is very strong with equations.

43
00:01:59,447 --> 00:02:01,977
He's much faster than I am
at calculations.

44
00:02:02,277 --> 00:02:04,487
And he's very smart.

45
00:02:04,487 --> 00:02:07,157
So I was hardly thinking about
the Deathmatch.

46
00:02:10,827 --> 00:02:11,887
I feel nervous.

47
00:02:13,357 --> 00:02:14,657
What's there to be nervous about?

48
00:02:15,057 --> 00:02:16,297
This is the kind of game
that makes me nervous.

49
00:02:16,427 --> 00:02:18,267
- Really?
- Yes.

50
00:02:18,727 --> 00:02:20,867
You'll be fine
as long as you don't lose your cool.

51
00:02:20,867 --> 00:02:24,637
I realized that some people
barely found anything.

52
00:02:24,737 --> 00:02:25,877
Even after running very hard.

53
00:02:26,977 --> 00:02:28,477
Even if you don't find much
at the beginning,

54
00:02:28,877 --> 00:02:30,807
the key is not to panic.

55
00:02:31,277 --> 00:02:33,247
No one in our alliance has
played it before.

56
00:02:33,847 --> 00:02:36,287
But hasn't everyone
on the other team done it already?

57
00:02:36,417 --> 00:02:38,287
- On the other team?
- I think all of them are experienced.

58
00:02:38,847 --> 00:02:41,017
- Everyone except Sang Min.
- Except Sang Min.

59
00:02:41,657 --> 00:02:43,757
Everyone except Sang Min has done it.

60
00:02:45,657 --> 00:02:46,957
I can't do it well without experience.

61
00:02:48,827 --> 00:02:50,197
Run simulations in your head.

62
00:02:50,367 --> 00:02:51,497
Yes, I've been doing that.

63
00:02:53,167 --> 00:02:54,167
Try this.

64
00:02:54,167 --> 00:02:56,907
- Write down random numbers.
- Okay.

65
00:02:57,937 --> 00:03:00,437
Then think about
how you'd approach them as a practice.

66
00:03:08,117 --> 00:03:09,787
One, nine, seven, six.

67
00:03:11,487 --> 00:03:13,217
I kept practicing calculations
over and over.

68
00:03:13,217 --> 00:03:14,387
Which numbers would be best,

69
00:03:14,387 --> 00:03:17,157
which symbols would work best.
I thought through all of that.

70
00:03:17,427 --> 00:03:18,487
This is the mindset you need.

71
00:03:19,087 --> 00:03:21,397
"Yes, this is my game. It's my moment."

72
00:03:21,857 --> 00:03:23,767
- "Kang Ji Hoo. That's me."
- Yes.

73
00:03:24,497 --> 00:03:25,937
"I'm here to show them."

74
00:03:25,937 --> 00:03:27,237
"I'll show you, you rascals."

75
00:03:28,637 --> 00:03:31,207
I was under a lot of pressure,

76
00:03:31,537 --> 00:03:33,577
but I kept acting confident.

77
00:03:33,877 --> 00:03:36,047
If I lost my confidence,

78
00:03:36,377 --> 00:03:37,947
my teammates would too.

79
00:03:38,407 --> 00:03:39,577
All of them were counting on me.

80
00:03:39,947 --> 00:03:42,217
I also had to intimidate the other team.

81
00:03:43,047 --> 00:03:46,287
I couldn't let anyone see me shaken.

82
00:03:48,687 --> 00:03:51,427
All players, please gather on the rooftop.

83
00:03:53,027 --> 00:03:54,597
Why are we starting on the rooftop...

84
00:03:54,757 --> 00:03:56,297
- instead of on the first floor?
- I don't know.

85
00:03:57,397 --> 00:04:00,967
We might start with the ones
on the rooftop or inside the pool.

86
00:04:03,167 --> 00:04:04,437
Who among us will go in?

87
00:04:04,607 --> 00:04:06,277
In Season Three, the pool was indoors.

88
00:04:06,777 --> 00:04:08,007
We'll see it from the inside, right?

89
00:04:09,277 --> 00:04:10,847
Everyone is staying in the building,
so there's probably nothing in the rooms.

90
00:04:10,847 --> 00:04:12,207
We don't see anything here either.

91
00:04:12,207 --> 00:04:14,177
- Ji Min, you're awake.
- Hello, Jin Ho.

92
00:04:14,177 --> 00:04:15,677
- Good luck.
- Are you feeling okay?

93
00:04:15,677 --> 00:04:17,817
Yes, let's send them home today. Darn it.

94
00:04:18,117 --> 00:04:19,147
Xitsuh, how is your hand?

95
00:04:19,657 --> 00:04:21,987
My hand is messed up. It's okay.

96
00:04:23,657 --> 00:04:24,957
Let's not get hurt this time.

97
00:04:32,737 --> 00:04:33,767
Are you going to run?

98
00:04:33,937 --> 00:04:35,197
- I'm screwed.
- Why?

99
00:04:35,667 --> 00:04:36,837
I don't think I can run.
I'm already exhausted.

100
00:04:37,807 --> 00:04:39,137
- You can do the calculations.
- I'm already tired.

101
00:04:39,137 --> 00:04:40,177
- What?
- You can do the calculations.

102
00:04:40,177 --> 00:04:42,177
We have plenty of human calculators
on our team. Why would I do that?

103
00:04:42,177 --> 00:04:43,907
- I'm like an old-school computer.
- I'm in charge of calculations.

104
00:04:43,907 --> 00:04:44,947
"Old-school computer?"

105
00:04:45,377 --> 00:04:46,617
- I'm in charge of it. Yes?
- Keun Woo.

106
00:04:46,717 --> 00:04:48,777
How should I describe you?

107
00:04:48,917 --> 00:04:49,947
You're not even a computer.

108
00:04:52,117 --> 00:04:53,117
Just run with me.

109
00:04:53,187 --> 00:04:54,857
We should listen to the rules first.

110
00:04:55,217 --> 00:04:57,427
We might have to run more than we think.

111
00:04:57,587 --> 00:04:59,427
- You can do it, right?
- Yes, you can count on me.

112
00:05:01,927 --> 00:05:03,067
- Our ace.
- He's our rising star.

113
00:05:03,067 --> 00:05:05,627
(The latest generation computer is here.)

114
00:05:05,867 --> 00:05:07,197
He's changed since yesterday.

115
00:05:07,197 --> 00:05:08,737
- He has changed.
- Since yesterday,

116
00:05:08,737 --> 00:05:10,567
- he's totally changed.
- How is it possible?

117
00:05:10,567 --> 00:05:12,207
When he gets an input,

118
00:05:12,337 --> 00:05:14,277
he comes up with the result immediately.

119
00:05:14,277 --> 00:05:15,277
He's amazing.

120
00:05:15,777 --> 00:05:16,847
Is your hand okay?

121
00:05:16,847 --> 00:05:17,907
(Sang Min arrives.)

122
00:05:17,907 --> 00:05:19,107
It's not a ligament injury, right?

123
00:05:19,177 --> 00:05:20,717
Are you okay? I'm so sorry.

124
00:05:26,417 --> 00:05:27,557
I wasn't thinking about it.

125
00:05:27,557 --> 00:05:28,817
But the moment I see his face,
I get annoyed.

126
00:05:29,657 --> 00:05:31,857
I don't want to see them.
We should send all of them home.

127
00:05:32,357 --> 00:05:33,857
I need to destroy them all.

128
00:05:34,727 --> 00:05:39,227
There was this odd tension
passing back and forth.

129
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:41,067
The vibe was a little off.

130
00:05:41,337 --> 00:05:43,167
Everyone wanted to take each other down.

131
00:05:43,167 --> 00:05:47,437
We all had that murderous look
in our eyes.

132
00:05:47,537 --> 00:05:49,207
Whatever role I play today,

133
00:05:49,207 --> 00:05:52,047
I'll do everything
to make sure my team wins.

134
00:05:52,177 --> 00:05:53,517
We will definitely win.

135
00:05:54,077 --> 00:05:56,447
Ji Hoo will handle the equations.

136
00:05:57,117 --> 00:06:00,557
If I focus on finding the tiles,
we have a good chance of winning.

137
00:06:02,087 --> 00:06:03,927
I feel reassured by everyone.

138
00:06:04,457 --> 00:06:06,357
- Let's destroy them with our skills.
- Our alliance team...

139
00:06:07,927 --> 00:06:09,567
Today's Money Challenge is...

140
00:06:09,797 --> 00:06:12,097
an alliance battle between two teams.

141
00:06:12,227 --> 00:06:13,737
The winning alliance team will receive...

142
00:06:13,737 --> 00:06:16,537
50,000 dollars in team fund...

143
00:06:16,967 --> 00:06:18,837
and an elimination immunity pass
for all members.

144
00:06:19,707 --> 00:06:22,777
The losing alliance team will become
elimination candidates...

145
00:06:23,177 --> 00:06:25,507
and must compete
in a team-on-team Deathmatch.

146
00:06:26,007 --> 00:06:28,017
All members of the losing team...

147
00:06:28,247 --> 00:06:30,187
- will be eliminated.
- All of us will survive.

148
00:06:31,247 --> 00:06:33,157
A whole team left yesterday,

149
00:06:33,157 --> 00:06:34,617
and now we're sending another one home?

150
00:06:35,317 --> 00:06:36,487
That's brutal.

151
00:06:36,557 --> 00:06:38,687
However, nothing has changed.

152
00:06:38,857 --> 00:06:40,327
There's no way I'm leaving today.

153
00:06:40,427 --> 00:06:41,957
I'm not going anywhere. Why?

154
00:06:42,497 --> 00:06:43,527
Because I need my revenge.

155
00:06:43,867 --> 00:06:45,397
I want to crush them.

156
00:06:45,397 --> 00:06:48,697
I've never wanted to destroy
an opponent this badly.

157
00:06:49,767 --> 00:06:50,967
It's exactly what I wanted.

158
00:06:51,507 --> 00:06:54,077
That team is so confident about this game.

159
00:06:54,077 --> 00:06:56,377
But they get completely destroyed,

160
00:06:56,907 --> 00:06:59,717
and they turn on each other in Deathmatch,
and one team goes home.

161
00:06:59,817 --> 00:07:01,117
How perfect would that be?

162
00:07:01,517 --> 00:07:03,817
For that to happen,
the most important thing is our victory.

163
00:07:03,917 --> 00:07:05,787
No matter what happens,

164
00:07:05,787 --> 00:07:08,087
we absolutely have to win today.

165
00:07:08,717 --> 00:07:11,957
Now I will reveal today's Money Challenge.

166
00:07:12,457 --> 00:07:14,027
Today's Money Challenge is...

167
00:07:15,257 --> 00:07:16,727
Equation Combo.

168
00:07:16,727 --> 00:07:18,627
(Equation Combo)

169
00:07:19,267 --> 00:07:22,297
Equation Combo is
a 2-on-2 alliance team battle.

170
00:07:22,637 --> 00:07:25,807
Players must place tiles containing
symbols and numbers onto the game board.

171
00:07:25,807 --> 00:07:27,037
- I see. Okay.
- They must create...

172
00:07:27,037 --> 00:07:29,107
as many combos as possible...

173
00:07:29,107 --> 00:07:31,507
where the equation equals a power of ten.

174
00:07:32,347 --> 00:07:35,377
Each alliance will have
two search players per round...

175
00:07:35,377 --> 00:07:37,947
who must locate hidden tile envelopes
scattered in the area.

176
00:07:38,717 --> 00:07:41,717
From Round 1 to 4, search time is...

177
00:07:41,887 --> 00:07:43,757
15 minutes per round.

178
00:07:46,557 --> 00:07:48,727
Round 5 lasts for 30 minutes.

179
00:07:49,057 --> 00:07:52,027
Players may only discard tiles
or pick up discarded tiles.

180
00:07:52,297 --> 00:07:54,437
After ten minutes have passed
in each round,

181
00:07:54,697 --> 00:07:56,607
no more tiles can be discarded.

182
00:07:56,607 --> 00:07:57,937
We have to discard all in ten minutes.

183
00:07:58,807 --> 00:08:01,077
Each alliance receives...

184
00:08:01,077 --> 00:08:04,177
a game board capable of holding 127 tiles.

185
00:08:05,107 --> 00:08:06,777
The hexagonal tiles contain...

186
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:09,117
both symbols and numbers.

187
00:08:09,117 --> 00:08:10,847
There are eight sets...

188
00:08:10,847 --> 00:08:13,157
of plus and minus tiles
numbered 1 through 9.

189
00:08:13,687 --> 00:08:16,787
There are 3 sets of multiplication tiles
numbered 1 through 5.

190
00:08:17,127 --> 00:08:20,857
And 4 sets of division tiles
numbered 1 through 4.

191
00:08:22,127 --> 00:08:24,497
Before the end of Round Five,

192
00:08:24,727 --> 00:08:27,637
each alliance must submit
their completed board to the butler.

193
00:08:28,097 --> 00:08:31,107
Once submitted,
the board can no longer be...

194
00:08:31,437 --> 00:08:32,707
checked or modified.

195
00:08:34,477 --> 00:08:36,977
After all alliances submit their boards,

196
00:08:37,277 --> 00:08:40,547
the alliance that submitted 1st will
attempt to complete their combos 1st.

197
00:08:40,777 --> 00:08:43,087
Combo completion takes place
in the Voting Room.

198
00:08:43,447 --> 00:08:45,847
Only one representative player
may participate.

199
00:08:45,987 --> 00:08:47,817
The time limit is 20 minutes.

200
00:08:47,817 --> 00:08:49,417
(Combo completion)

201
00:08:50,187 --> 00:08:52,897
During this stage,
no writing instruments are allowed.

202
00:08:53,897 --> 00:08:55,997
- Yes.
- Players may not mark...

203
00:08:56,267 --> 00:08:57,327
- the tiles...
- It's mental math.

204
00:08:57,327 --> 00:08:59,397
- Be quiet.
- or the game board...

205
00:08:59,397 --> 00:09:00,767
- in any way.
- They're being so cocky.

206
00:09:01,197 --> 00:09:02,267
Is he good at mental math?

207
00:09:02,267 --> 00:09:03,837
You must complete combos...

208
00:09:03,837 --> 00:09:05,467
- relying only on your memory.
- He's so excited already.

209
00:09:06,737 --> 00:09:09,037
Here are the rules for completing a combo.

210
00:09:09,377 --> 00:09:11,507
Each team is given one piece to use...

211
00:09:11,507 --> 00:09:13,247
for completing combos.

212
00:09:13,777 --> 00:09:16,917
A player chooses one of the tiles
placed on the game board...

213
00:09:17,117 --> 00:09:19,887
as the starting tile
and places the piece on it.

214
00:09:19,987 --> 00:09:22,287
They move the piece to adjacent tiles...

215
00:09:22,487 --> 00:09:24,127
while continuously calculating...

216
00:09:24,127 --> 00:09:25,587
the equations written on each tile.

217
00:09:26,227 --> 00:09:29,997
However, a tile that has already been
visited cannot be visited again.

218
00:09:30,827 --> 00:09:32,937
The symbol attached
to the starting tile is...

219
00:09:32,937 --> 00:09:34,697
excluded from the calculation.

220
00:09:34,967 --> 00:09:37,507
Normal mathematical order
of operations does not apply.

221
00:09:37,767 --> 00:09:40,477
Calculations must be performed strictly
in the order the tiles are visited.

222
00:09:41,407 --> 00:09:44,407
Players may stop
moving the piece at any point...

223
00:09:44,577 --> 00:09:46,477
and declare a combo completion.

224
00:09:46,977 --> 00:09:49,617
If the final value of the completed
equation is a power of ten,

225
00:09:49,887 --> 00:09:51,087
such as ten,

226
00:09:51,187 --> 00:09:53,757
100, 1,000, or 10,000,

227
00:09:53,917 --> 00:09:55,687
the combo is considered completed.

228
00:09:55,987 --> 00:09:57,027
Goodness.

229
00:09:57,987 --> 00:09:59,727
If a player successfully completes
a combo,

230
00:09:59,857 --> 00:10:02,697
the starting tile of that combo is
removed from the board.

231
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:06,537
The final tile where the piece landed
becomes the new starting tile,

232
00:10:06,637 --> 00:10:08,667
allowing the player
to attempt another combo.

233
00:10:10,137 --> 00:10:12,537
The scoring system is as follows.

234
00:10:13,237 --> 00:10:16,207
Each combo's score is calculated
by multiplying the number of tiles...

235
00:10:16,777 --> 00:10:19,777
used to complete the combo
by the number of zeros contained...

236
00:10:20,047 --> 00:10:22,177
in the final equation value.

237
00:10:22,947 --> 00:10:26,387
After adding up the scores
from all completed combos,

238
00:10:26,857 --> 00:10:29,627
points are deducted based on
the number of unused tiles remaining.

239
00:10:29,987 --> 00:10:32,557
The resulting score is then multiplied
by the number of completed combos.

240
00:10:32,887 --> 00:10:35,027
Finally, 100 bonus points are added...

241
00:10:35,027 --> 00:10:37,197
to the team that created
the longest combo,

242
00:10:37,467 --> 00:10:39,527
determining each team's final score.

243
00:10:40,097 --> 00:10:42,797
The two teams belonging to the alliance
with the lower final score...

244
00:10:43,037 --> 00:10:45,637
will face each other
in a team-versus-team Deathmatch.

245
00:10:46,777 --> 00:10:49,577
There are three types of items
that can be used in the Equation Combo.

246
00:10:50,077 --> 00:10:53,217
The first item is plus ten tile.

247
00:10:53,647 --> 00:10:56,077
It can be added to your equation
during calculation.

248
00:10:56,587 --> 00:10:59,317
The second item is extra searcher.

249
00:10:59,787 --> 00:11:02,857
It allows one extra player to participate
in the search during the next round.

250
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:05,857
The third item is a hidden item.

251
00:11:06,057 --> 00:11:08,197
It will be revealed before
the start of Round Four.

252
00:11:09,197 --> 00:11:11,867
Soon, the game will start.

253
00:11:12,267 --> 00:11:13,767
Each alliance must decide...

254
00:11:13,767 --> 00:11:16,567
