in the farthest spot.

636
00:27:40,917 --> 00:27:44,887
My plan was to sweep the entire area,
starting from the farthest corner.

637
00:27:46,627 --> 00:27:48,627
Oh, my. Beom has made it
to an incredibly distant spot.

638
00:27:48,627 --> 00:27:50,627
I hope he finds a lot of tiles
so that all his hard work pays off.

639
00:28:06,507 --> 00:28:09,417
(He has a keen eye too.)

640
00:28:28,097 --> 00:28:31,307
(Kwak Beom has already cleared out
the outdoor search zone.)

641
00:28:35,307 --> 00:28:37,007
Gosh. I don't see many tiles outside.

642
00:28:38,107 --> 00:28:40,847
(Jeong Keun Woo heads back up
after finding one tile.)

643
00:28:41,177 --> 00:28:43,617
Keun Woo arrived late
and missed all the tiles.

644
00:28:44,747 --> 00:28:47,387
(Kwak Beom made it to the back corner
ahead of his opponent team.)

645
00:28:52,327 --> 00:28:54,457
Heading straight there first was
a brilliant idea.

646
00:28:54,457 --> 00:28:55,927
- It was a good strategy.
- Indeed.

647
00:28:55,927 --> 00:28:57,097
I think he found 3 or 4 tiles...

648
00:28:57,097 --> 00:28:58,097
- in that garden area alone.
- Right.

649
00:29:04,967 --> 00:29:06,407
Then that brings the total to three.

650
00:29:06,567 --> 00:29:09,277
So I'll place one "multiply three" tile
right here.

651
00:29:09,277 --> 00:29:10,807
And number one goes to the end...

652
00:29:10,807 --> 00:29:13,177
Wait, but number one won't work
in this equation.

653
00:29:13,177 --> 00:29:15,917
It should be bigger than minus three.

654
00:29:15,917 --> 00:29:17,417
- He's in the zone.
- Sorry?

655
00:29:18,447 --> 00:29:19,617
Xitsuh is completely in the zone again.

656
00:29:19,917 --> 00:29:21,517
Yes, he's in the zone.
We must not go near him.

657
00:29:21,857 --> 00:29:24,927
- He's in the zone.
- He's in a good state right now.

658
00:29:25,357 --> 00:29:27,557
Xitsuh, all we have to do now is...

659
00:29:28,157 --> 00:29:31,427
