They found so many tiles.

742
00:34:37,067 --> 00:34:38,107
Exactly.

743
00:34:38,637 --> 00:34:39,737
That's okay. We'll find even more tiles.

744
00:34:39,737 --> 00:34:41,007
It's easy to find many tiles
in the beginning.

745
00:34:41,907 --> 00:34:43,807
- Gosh, it's a mess.
- This is awesome.

746
00:34:46,447 --> 00:34:48,117
- Here you go. Have some water.
- Hey, that's a lot.

747
00:34:48,117 --> 00:34:50,317
- Hey, they found so many tiles.
- Exactly.

748
00:34:50,917 --> 00:34:52,117
My goodness. This is amazing.

749
00:34:52,117 --> 00:34:53,187
- It's awesome.
- Which places did you search?

750
00:34:53,817 --> 00:34:55,317
(Sang Min naturally joins them.)

751
00:34:55,317 --> 00:34:56,357
Slow down.

752
00:34:56,487 --> 00:34:59,627
- Shall I sort the tiles by symbols?
- Yes, we'll sort the tiles now.

753
00:35:00,127 --> 00:35:01,357
Place the addition tiles on the right.

754
00:35:01,827 --> 00:35:02,857
Place the subtraction tiles over here.

755
00:35:03,257 --> 00:35:04,567
Oh, we have a lot of subtraction tiles.

756
00:35:05,067 --> 00:35:06,527
- Oh, no.
- It's okay.

757
00:35:14,507 --> 00:35:17,577
(Jotting)

758
00:35:18,907 --> 00:35:21,677
These are subtraction tiles,
and these are addition tiles.

759
00:35:21,677 --> 00:35:23,177
- They got so many subtraction tiles.
- Yes.

760
00:35:23,177 --> 00:35:24,647
Subtraction tiles are useless.

761
00:35:25,287 --> 00:35:26,447
- Four and four?
- Yes.

762
00:35:26,547 --> 00:35:28,687
- Were you born in 1992?
- They found these tiles.

763
00:35:28,687 --> 00:35:30,457
Almost all subtraction tiles
have been found.

764
00:35:30,457 --> 00:35:31,557
This is good for us.

765
00:35:31,557 --> 00:35:32,757
How do you know that?

766
00:35:33,157 --> 00:35:34,257
He saw their tiles.

767
00:35:34,457 --> 00:35:35,657
Thank you so much.

768
00:35:35,657 --> 00:35:38,627
From here on, it's all downhill for them.

769
00:35:40,597 --> 00:35:42,997
(Jeong Keun Woo of the search team
returns.)

770
00:35:42,997 --> 00:35:44,137
- Did you find a lot?
- Hey, didn't you find a lot?

771
00:35:44,137 --> 00:35:45,307
There weren't many in the outdoor zone.

772
00:35:45,307 --> 00:35:46,967
That's okay. I saw that they overlapped.

773
00:35:48,137 --> 00:35:49,137
(Park Ji Min)

774
00:35:49,507 --> 00:35:52,107
Hey, this is a lot.
You found a lot of tiles.

775
00:35:52,107 --> 00:35:53,777
- I found 17 tiles.
- You found 17 tiles?

776
00:35:53,777 --> 00:35:55,817
- That's a lot. Awesome.
- He found a lot.

777
00:35:56,547 --> 00:35:58,747
- What is that one?
- We have a lot of addition tiles.

778
00:35:58,747 --> 00:35:59,787
All of these are addition tiles.

779
00:35:59,787 --> 00:36:02,117
- Oh, my. That's amazing.
- Quiet down.

780
00:36:02,187 --> 00:36:05,227
Keun Woo, great job. Thank you so much.

781
00:36:05,227 --> 00:36:06,387
Let's just use these tiles
and not search for more.

782
00:36:07,057 --> 00:36:10,257
Addition tiles practically poured down
from above.

783
00:36:10,297 --> 00:36:11,827
This is what it felt like.

784
00:36:11,827 --> 00:36:14,097
Like the universe approved of our plan
and said, "Go ahead with it."

785
00:36:14,497 --> 00:36:17,167
- I couldn't find a lot.
- That's okay. Great job.

786
00:36:17,497 --> 00:36:18,637
I found 34 tiles.

787
00:36:18,637 --> 00:36:20,967
That's insane. Is that even possible?

788
00:36:21,477 --> 00:36:22,677
Let's take a look at them.

789
00:36:24,337 --> 00:36:25,977
- Isn't this insane?
- It's insane.

790
00:36:25,977 --> 00:36:28,547
Tae Gyun, in particular, amazed me.
It felt like he was performing magic.

791
00:36:28,547 --> 00:36:30,047
Countless tiles just poured out
of his pouch.

792
00:36:30,147 --> 00:36:32,117
Finding plenty of tiles in the beginning
gives you an advantage.

793
00:36:32,117 --> 00:36:34,047
Because if you find a lot of tiles
in the later rounds,

794
00:36:34,047 --> 00:36:36,687
it causes you to spend more time
arranging the tiles.

795
00:36:36,687 --> 00:36:39,557
In that sense, it turned out
to be a great outcome for my team.

796
00:36:40,427 --> 00:36:42,397
I couldn't find a single tile.

797
00:36:43,657 --> 00:36:45,127
- You didn't find a single tile?
- No.

798
00:36:45,127 --> 00:36:46,127
Darn.

799
00:36:46,127 --> 00:36:47,197
Where should I place them?

800
00:36:47,597 --> 00:36:49,367
- But you don't have any.
- I have no tiles, not even one.

801
00:36:52,407 --> 00:36:53,467
Beom is incredible.

802
00:36:55,077 --> 00:36:57,207
Hold on. Where should I place these tiles?

803
00:36:57,207 --> 00:36:58,307
Right where we placed the tiles earlier.

804
00:37:00,147 --> 00:37:01,217
Who will go next?

805
00:37:01,217 --> 00:37:02,777
- Me.
- These three, including you.

806
00:37:02,777 --> 00:37:03,847
- Seung Yong?
- Yes.

807
00:37:03,847 --> 00:37:05,317
- And?
- Me and...

808
00:37:05,317 --> 00:37:07,447
(Searchers for Round 2:
Kwak Beom, Hyun Sung Joo, Shin Seung Yong)

809
00:37:07,447 --> 00:37:08,757
You don't have to search the area...

810
00:37:08,757 --> 00:37:10,617
- Where?
- that's far from here.

811
00:37:10,617 --> 00:37:11,927
- I swept that area clean.
- Really?

812
00:37:11,927 --> 00:37:13,957
There's no tile left there.
I searched really thoroughly.

813
00:37:14,187 --> 00:37:16,857
- I searched the rooms.
- I see.

814
00:37:16,857 --> 00:37:18,567
You'll have to spend more time
searching the rooms than you think.

815
00:37:19,367 --> 00:37:21,937
Who are up next?
Seong Beom and Xitsuh are up next.

816
00:37:22,197 --> 00:37:24,237
I searched the rooms
on the third floor twice. Don't go there.

817
00:37:24,497 --> 00:37:27,637
- Round Two will now begin.
- Run.

818
00:37:27,637 --> 00:37:29,737
(Equation Combo, Round 2,
Remaining tiles: 82)

819
00:37:29,737 --> 00:37:31,037
I'll go search the main hall.

820
00:37:32,647 --> 00:37:33,747
Let's be careful not to get hurt.

821
00:37:33,747 --> 00:37:37,717
(The total number of searchers
for Round 2 is 6.)

822
00:37:43,657 --> 00:37:47,227
(Shin Seung Yong and Heo Seong Beom
search the cafeteria.)

823
00:38:04,377 --> 00:38:05,477
Oh, my gosh.

824
00:38:05,477 --> 00:38:07,007
(The remaining 4 run
in the same direction.)

825
00:38:07,007 --> 00:38:09,717
(The locations of tiles)

826
00:38:19,057 --> 00:38:22,427
(With his keen eye, he finds the tiles
that everyone else overlooked.)

827
00:38:26,567 --> 00:38:29,837
(Team P1's room)

828
00:38:32,567 --> 00:38:35,737
(Team P3's room)

829
00:38:36,537 --> 00:38:40,677
In the first round,
I couldn't cover all the rooms entirely.

830
00:38:40,747 --> 00:38:42,547
(Team P3's room)

831
00:38:42,547 --> 00:38:45,817
In Round 2, I searched the rooms
I couldn't cover in Round 1,

832
00:38:46,387 --> 00:38:49,557
(Seung Yong searches as thoroughly
as Beom did.)

833
00:38:49,987 --> 00:38:51,627
the main hall,
and the outside of the main hall.

834
00:38:51,627 --> 00:38:53,357
I only searched those areas.

835
00:39:00,397 --> 00:39:02,897
You see, in the first round,

836
00:39:02,997 --> 00:39:05,667
we already found a total of 51 tiles...

837
00:39:05,667 --> 00:39:08,137
- out of 175 tiles.
- We found a lot of tiles.

838
00:39:08,277 --> 00:39:11,037
- We found almost 30 percent.
- Yes.

839
00:39:14,507 --> 00:39:16,277
Which type of tiles do we have the most?

840
00:39:16,277 --> 00:39:17,377
(Hye Seon mapped out a complete table
of the equation tiles.)

841
00:39:17,377 --> 00:39:18,387
We have more addition tiles
than any other type.

842
00:39:18,387 --> 00:39:20,917
Are we allowed to arrange the tiles now?
Will they come and see...

843
00:39:22,857 --> 00:39:23,857
Don't come here.

844
00:39:24,287 --> 00:39:26,127
How are we supposed to see them
when you flipped them all over?

845
00:39:28,757 --> 00:39:30,357
- We put ours right side up.
- This is my today's mission.

846
00:39:30,357 --> 00:39:32,567
Today, I can't run, search,

847
00:39:32,567 --> 00:39:34,197
or calculate, so I need to defend well.

848
00:39:34,197 --> 00:39:35,897
Have you been learning
how to play basketball from Gwan Hee?

849
00:39:36,267 --> 00:39:37,337
What are you talking about?

850
00:39:37,337 --> 00:39:38,567
Are you blocking me?

851
00:39:40,907 --> 00:39:42,407
You already flipped it,
so there's nothing for me to see.

852
00:39:42,407 --> 00:39:43,807
We'll be doing something now.

853
00:39:44,607 --> 00:39:46,177
You flipped it and blocked me from it,

854
00:39:46,177 --> 00:39:47,647
so what am I supposed to see?

855
00:39:47,647 --> 00:39:50,217
There's nothing to see, so turn around.

856
00:39:50,317 --> 00:39:51,717
Go back to your place.

857
00:39:52,087 --> 00:39:54,287
Isn't it our territory until here?

858
00:39:54,287 --> 00:39:55,987
Is it? Should we draw a line here?

859
00:39:57,487 --> 00:39:58,987
I'll combine 1 and 9.

860
00:39:59,187 --> 00:40:00,857
One and nine.

861
00:40:05,397 --> 00:40:07,997
If we get a plus one tile,
that goes here, Hye Seon.

862
00:40:08,097 --> 00:40:09,467
- Got it?
- Okay.

863
00:40:11,037 --> 00:40:12,707
(Meanwhile, Team Indoor Alliance)

864
00:40:19,407 --> 00:40:21,677
You haven't started combining, right?
Let me know when you do.

865
00:40:21,677 --> 00:40:22,777
I'll check it with you.

866
00:40:23,847 --> 00:40:25,547
I'm just practicing.

867
00:40:26,847 --> 00:40:28,717
Things didn't look good in the beginning.

868
00:40:28,857 --> 00:40:31,157
The minus tiles are of little use.

869
00:40:31,157 --> 00:40:33,427
They'll make negative numbers.

870
00:40:33,427 --> 00:40:36,197
But we need to make positive numbers,
10, 100, 1,000, 10,000, and so on.

871
00:40:36,397 --> 00:40:37,957
I started to get nervous.

872
00:40:39,767 --> 00:40:41,797
If you multiply a negative number,

873
00:40:42,337 --> 00:40:43,737
there's no way to save yourself from it.

874
00:40:43,837 --> 00:40:45,367
If you multiply a negative number...

875
00:40:45,367 --> 00:40:48,037
(Ji Hoo is stuck
because of the abundant minus tiles.)

876
00:40:48,307 --> 00:40:49,777
I need to make a positive number...

877
00:40:51,007 --> 00:40:52,547
before they come back.

878
00:40:59,217 --> 00:41:00,517
Darn it.

879
00:41:02,717 --> 00:41:04,457
In Round One,
when we saw from the rooftop,

880
00:41:04,457 --> 00:41:06,427
we could see certain places...

881
00:41:06,427 --> 00:41:08,857
which would be good to search.

882
00:41:09,257 --> 00:41:12,197
They asked me
to search the room one more time.

883
00:41:12,197 --> 00:41:14,167
(Team P2's room)

884
00:41:17,397 --> 00:41:19,037
I went, and there was nothing.

885
00:41:24,207 --> 00:41:27,607
When you come back
and your pockets aren't full,

886
00:41:27,607 --> 00:41:28,747
you feel self-conscious.

887
00:41:28,747 --> 00:41:30,017
It looks like you didn't work hard enough.

888
00:41:30,017 --> 00:41:31,787
But that's not true. I really did my best.

889
00:41:40,257 --> 00:41:43,827
(He acquires 2.)

890
00:41:43,857 --> 00:41:46,797
When I ran down for Round Two, they said,

891
00:41:46,927 --> 00:41:48,567
"Don't bother searching
on the third floor."

892
00:41:48,897 --> 00:41:50,567
"We've thoroughly searched the main hall."

893
00:41:50,897 --> 00:41:53,407
"There was nothing much outdoors."

894
00:41:53,407 --> 00:41:54,767
With that information, I set off.

895
00:41:56,937 --> 00:42:00,177
I went to the first floor,
where my room was.

896
00:42:00,177 --> 00:42:01,307
(Team P3's room)

897
00:42:01,307 --> 00:42:02,617
I went to the first floor...

898
00:42:02,617 --> 00:42:04,847
and searched my room, Team P3's room.

899
00:42:04,847 --> 00:42:09,117
(Tile hidden)

900
00:42:15,227 --> 00:42:18,797
(Tile hidden)

901
00:42:18,797 --> 00:42:20,597
What's this?

902
00:42:20,697 --> 00:42:22,697
There was nothing at all.

903
00:42:23,137 --> 00:42:25,667
I even opened the microwave.

904
00:42:25,807 --> 00:42:27,367
I opened the fridge too.

905
00:42:27,367 --> 00:42:28,577
Nothing.

906
00:42:29,337 --> 00:42:30,477
(Team C's room)

907
00:42:30,477 --> 00:42:31,747
There's nothing.

908
00:42:33,547 --> 00:42:35,217
Darn it.

909
00:42:35,217 --> 00:42:36,377
Where is it?

910
00:42:36,377 --> 00:42:38,387
I went to Team C's room too. Nothing.

911
00:42:38,517 --> 00:42:40,417
I went to Team P1's room too. Nothing.

912
00:42:40,417 --> 00:42:42,057
(Tiles hidden)

913
00:42:46,087 --> 00:42:48,997
(The tiles Xitsuh failed to find)

914
00:42:51,597 --> 00:42:53,697
(Team Indoor Alliance finds them.)

915
00:42:53,897 --> 00:42:55,637
I'm screwed.

916
00:42:57,237 --> 00:42:58,737
I normally...

917
00:42:59,067 --> 00:43:00,207
I mean,

918
00:43:00,467 --> 00:43:03,207
in the previous seasons,
I was good at finding them.

919
00:43:03,207 --> 00:43:04,407
But there was nothing.

920
00:43:04,807 --> 00:43:06,847
There was nothing at all.

921
00:43:08,107 --> 00:43:10,077
So I went outdoor.

922
00:43:11,117 --> 00:43:13,747
I checked the flowerbed and so on.

923
00:43:13,747 --> 00:43:16,417
I even thought about entering
an unknown building.

924
00:43:18,117 --> 00:43:19,687
This doesn't make sense.

925
00:43:21,157 --> 00:43:25,227
(Xitsuh heads outside.)

926
00:43:25,997 --> 00:43:29,867
(Jeong Keun Woo, who is on the same team,
is already searching there.)

927
00:43:30,837 --> 00:43:33,137
There's nothing here. Go up.

928
00:43:33,737 --> 00:43:35,707
This is impossible, Keun Woo.

929
00:43:35,777 --> 00:43:37,107
The rooms on the second floor...

930
00:43:37,107 --> 00:43:38,307
There's no tiles in the room either.

931
00:43:38,307 --> 00:43:39,577
- Really?
- Yes.

932
00:43:40,477 --> 00:43:42,617
Xitsuh, you go up here.
I'll go through here and join you.

933
00:43:52,327 --> 00:43:54,487
Xitsuh, there's nothing there.
Go back inside the building.

934
00:43:54,487 --> 00:43:56,057
The chances are slim out here.

935
00:43:56,257 --> 00:43:57,297
Okay, Keun Woo.

936
00:43:58,157 --> 00:43:59,927
Xitsuh, gosh...

937
00:44:00,597 --> 00:44:02,697
I keep telling him...

938
00:44:02,697 --> 00:44:04,167
to search indoors,

939
00:44:04,267 --> 00:44:05,537
so why is he outside?

940
00:44:05,737 --> 00:44:07,067
"No, Xitsuh, I've searched there."

941
00:44:07,067 --> 00:44:08,907
"Okay, Keun Woo."

942
00:44:08,907 --> 00:44:11,107
He says that, so why?

943
00:44:11,407 --> 00:44:12,907
Go back up. I'll have a look here.

944
00:44:12,907 --> 00:44:13,947
- I'll go back up first.
- Yes.

945
00:44:13,947 --> 00:44:15,717
- Go up.
- Have you gone up here?

946
00:44:15,817 --> 00:44:17,217
You can't. There's a barricade.

947
00:44:17,217 --> 00:44:18,317
Okay, Keun Woo.

948
00:44:19,117 --> 00:44:20,917
"Xitsuh, go back in." "Okay, Keun Woo."

949
00:44:20,917 --> 00:44:22,017
And I run into him again.

950
00:44:22,017 --> 00:44:23,517
He wasted all the time like that.

951
00:44:23,587 --> 00:44:25,227
Xitsuh is a total mess.

952
00:44:25,927 --> 00:44:28,157
Let me just find one.

953
00:44:28,627 --> 00:44:29,757
Just one.

954
00:44:29,797 --> 00:44:31,257
I want to see how it looks like.

955
00:44:36,237 --> 00:44:37,297
Three.

956
00:44:37,297 --> 00:44:38,737
(Seong Beom is searching by the pool.)

957
00:44:42,507 --> 00:44:43,677
No.

958
00:44:43,677 --> 00:44:45,047
Where is it?

959
00:44:45,507 --> 00:44:48,377
They left all these goodies here?

960
00:44:49,517 --> 00:44:51,147
I went to the flowerbed
by the swimming pool...

961
00:44:51,147 --> 00:44:52,217
and checked every corner.

962
00:44:52,217 --> 00:44:53,717
So many of them had been there.

963
00:44:53,717 --> 00:44:56,317
"I hit the jackpot."

964
00:44:56,387 --> 00:44:58,257
I picked up a lot there.

965
00:45:04,027 --> 00:45:06,267
After that, I headed outdoors.

966
00:45:06,697 --> 00:45:09,537
Keun Woo clearly told me
there wasn't much outdoors.

967
00:45:09,537 --> 00:45:11,297
I should've listened to him.

968
00:45:12,267 --> 00:45:14,367
Outdoors...

969
00:45:16,677 --> 00:45:18,707
(Outdoor search zone)

970
00:45:18,707 --> 00:45:19,747
Let's go.

971
00:45:23,417 --> 00:45:26,687
(Seong Beom follows the path
Xitsuh has taken before him.)

972
00:45:26,687 --> 00:45:28,817
I thought,
"Maybe he just couldn't find them,"

973
00:45:28,817 --> 00:45:30,487
and went on a search.

974
00:45:31,787 --> 00:45:33,127
How come there's nothing at all?

975
00:45:34,357 --> 00:45:35,927
People wouldn't have gone here yet.

976
00:45:38,827 --> 00:45:40,527
There really wasn't any.

977
00:45:40,797 --> 00:45:45,137
I ran around so much outdoors,

978
00:45:45,167 --> 00:45:46,607
but I couldn't spot any.

979
00:45:46,637 --> 00:45:47,837
Why is there nothing?

980
00:45:48,267 --> 00:45:49,577
This is insane.

981
00:45:51,947 --> 00:45:53,477
There's nothing outside?

982
00:45:54,277 --> 00:45:55,447
Come on.

983
00:45:55,547 --> 00:45:56,847
This doesn't make sense.

984
00:46:00,087 --> 00:46:02,687
Five minutes before the search ends.

985
00:46:02,687 --> 00:46:06,127
(Equation Combo, Round 2)

986
00:46:09,757 --> 00:46:11,797
How is this possible?

987
00:46:12,427 --> 00:46:13,727
I couldn't find anything.

988
00:46:13,767 --> 00:46:14,897
This was a first.

989
00:46:17,737 --> 00:46:19,437
They say better safe than sorry...

990
00:46:19,537 --> 00:46:20,667
and that it's right under your nose.

991
00:46:20,667 --> 00:46:22,277
So I went to the main hall.

992
00:46:32,547 --> 00:46:36,857
(Tile hidden)

993
00:46:37,017 --> 00:46:38,217
In the pantry,

994
00:46:38,217 --> 00:46:41,157
behind a sofa,
there was one in plain sight.

995
00:46:41,487 --> 00:46:43,727
What's this?
Zero and one are very different.

996
00:46:43,727 --> 00:46:45,057
If you bring back zero tile,

997
00:46:45,627 --> 00:46:47,327
it could mean
you'd simply lied around somewhere.

998
00:46:47,567 --> 00:46:50,797
If you bring back one,
it shows that you've at least tried.

999
00:46:50,837 --> 00:46:52,337
Someone might've dropped it.

1000
00:46:54,537 --> 00:46:56,607
Thankfully, I picked that one up.

1001
00:46:58,137 --> 00:47:01,077
Three minutes until the search ends.

1002
00:47:01,077 --> 00:47:02,677
(Equation Combo, Round 2)

1003
00:47:08,787 --> 00:47:10,887
This round isn't easy.

1004
00:47:17,557 --> 00:47:18,667
Where are you?

1005
00:47:18,867 --> 00:47:20,097
Tiles, where are you?

1006
00:47:20,827 --> 00:47:21,997
Come on.

1007
00:47:22,097 --> 00:47:23,667
How come you're nowhere to be seen?

1008
00:47:24,937 --> 00:47:26,767
Seong Beom, we have one minute left.

1009
00:47:26,767 --> 00:47:27,967
Okay.

1010
00:47:29,577 --> 00:47:32,577
One minute until the search ends.

1011
00:47:32,577 --> 00:47:34,507
(Equation Combo, Round 2)

1012
00:47:37,717 --> 00:47:42,417
(The searchers hurry back
to the Voting Room at the announcement.)

1013
00:47:47,457 --> 00:47:48,727
This is so darn exhausting.

1014
00:47:50,627 --> 00:47:52,897
Round Two has ended.

1015
00:47:52,897 --> 00:47:53,897
(Round 2 has ended.)

1016
00:47:53,897 --> 00:47:57,067
Round 3 will commence after 10 minutes.

1017
00:48:01,507 --> 00:48:03,877
Team Indoor Alliance,
will you register the tiles?

1018
00:48:05,207 --> 00:48:07,607
You have registered 11 tiles.

1019
00:48:08,447 --> 00:48:09,817
You have registered eight tiles.

1020
00:48:09,817 --> 00:48:11,647
- I'll bring them back.
- Yes, please.

1021
00:48:13,887 --> 00:48:15,857
You have registered two tiles.

1022
00:48:15,857 --> 00:48:17,757
Can I buy an item now?

1023
00:48:17,757 --> 00:48:19,427
Which item would you like to buy?

1024
00:48:19,627 --> 00:48:20,787
A plus 10 tile.

1025
00:48:21,727 --> 00:48:24,257
For Team Rookie, 10,000 dollars
will be deducted from the team funds.

1026
00:48:24,257 --> 00:48:25,767
(Plus 10 tile purchased)

1027
00:48:25,767 --> 00:48:27,697
(Team Indoor Alliance,
Round 2 tile status)

1028
00:48:27,697 --> 00:48:29,667
(Team Indoor Alliance, 64 tiles)

1029
00:48:30,467 --> 00:48:32,337
Multiply by four tile.

1030
00:48:32,437 --> 00:48:34,537
You have found one tile.

1031
00:48:34,537 --> 00:48:36,507
- Would you like to register it?
- Yes, please.

1032
00:48:36,707 --> 00:48:38,537
You have registered two tiles.

1033
00:48:38,537 --> 00:48:39,647
Thanks.

1034
00:48:40,277 --> 00:48:41,407
Heo Seong Beom,

1035
00:48:41,407 --> 00:48:44,117
you have joined the queue
after the round has ended.

1036
00:48:44,217 --> 00:48:46,647
- You cannot register the tiles anymore.
- Really?

1037
00:48:46,717 --> 00:48:48,117
You can keep it to yourself...

1038
00:48:48,117 --> 00:48:50,187
and hand it over
to the next round's player.

1039
00:48:50,187 --> 00:48:51,287
I understand.

1040
00:48:52,057 --> 00:48:53,687
What's the use of running around
to find them?

1041
00:48:53,687 --> 00:48:54,957
I couldn't register them.

1042
00:48:54,957 --> 00:48:56,797
They became useless.

1043
00:48:56,797 --> 00:48:58,667
(Team Outdoor Alliance,
Round 2 tile status)

1044
00:48:58,667 --> 00:49:00,667
(Team Outdoor Alliance, 54 tiles)

1045
00:49:00,827 --> 00:49:01,937
Good job.

1046
00:49:02,037 --> 00:49:03,697
Good job.

1047
00:49:04,667 --> 00:49:06,467
I barely could find anything. I found one.

1048
00:49:06,467 --> 00:49:07,667
- It's okay.
- You worked hard.

1049
00:49:07,667 --> 00:49:09,137
- It's okay.
- Good job.

1050
00:49:09,137 --> 00:49:10,807
- Did you search the first-floor rooms?
- I did.

1051
00:49:10,807 --> 00:49:12,007
- There was nothing?
- Nothing.

1052
00:49:12,377 --> 00:49:13,407
I even opened...

1053
00:49:13,407 --> 00:49:14,447
- the fridge and the microwave.
- Where else can we go, then?

1054
00:49:14,477 --> 00:49:15,617
There's nowhere to go.

1055
00:49:15,617 --> 00:49:16,947
I opened everything.

1056
00:49:16,947 --> 00:49:18,417
Good job, Seong Beom.

1057
00:49:19,347 --> 00:49:21,317
- I found seven.
- Yes.

1058
00:49:21,347 --> 00:49:23,487
But I queued up two seconds late,
so they didn't let me register this round.

1059
00:49:23,487 --> 00:49:24,517
You need to register them
in the next round.

1060
00:49:24,517 --> 00:49:25,527
Really?

1061
00:49:25,627 --> 00:49:27,457
It's okay,
we have plenty of time to calculate.

1062
00:49:29,197 --> 00:49:30,397
There's nothing.

1063
00:49:31,127 --> 00:49:32,727
I couldn't find one.

1064
00:49:33,727 --> 00:49:34,827
But you found two, right?

1065
00:49:38,707 --> 00:49:39,837
Darn it.

1066
00:49:40,237 --> 00:49:41,767
We're running out of tiles now.

1067
00:49:42,177 --> 00:49:43,207
We can do it.

1068
00:49:43,307 --> 00:49:45,037
- You can do it, Beom.
- Yes, let's run two more times.

1069
00:49:45,307 --> 00:49:46,377
This is so fun.

1070
00:49:47,107 --> 00:49:49,277
Round Three starts now.

1071
00:49:50,217 --> 00:49:52,187
(Equation Combo, Round 3,
Remaining tiles: 51)

1072
00:49:52,187 --> 00:49:54,047
- Let's do this.
- Run slowly.

1073
00:50:16,677 --> 00:50:17,807
There really isn't any.

1074
00:50:18,677 --> 00:50:20,977
We've more or less run out of
the tiles left to find.

1075
00:50:21,407 --> 00:50:23,347
What if I can't find any?

1076
00:50:23,977 --> 00:50:25,317
So I ran downstairs.

1077
00:50:27,047 --> 00:50:28,147
Isn't that a tile?

1078
00:50:30,217 --> 00:50:32,287
Guess what? There were...

1079
00:50:32,287 --> 00:50:34,987
multiple tiles hanging on the trees
by the swimming pool.

1080
00:50:35,827 --> 00:50:36,827
Darn it.

1081
00:50:41,097 --> 00:50:44,837
So I jumped and pulled down
the three tiles.

1082
00:50:48,207 --> 00:50:50,307
And I started crawling around in the room.

1083
00:50:57,547 --> 00:50:59,447
I found two more like that.

1084
00:51:00,517 --> 00:51:02,557
(Seung Yong is searching outdoors.)

1085
00:51:18,837 --> 00:51:20,807
(He searches thoroughly
in case he missed out on any.)

1086
00:51:25,207 --> 00:51:27,047
(Kwak Beom is good at searching as ever.)

1087
00:51:52,907 --> 00:51:55,267
Darn it. There's nothing.

1088
00:52:10,757 --> 00:52:11,787
Goodness.

1089
00:52:12,527 --> 00:52:13,557
Darn it.

1090
00:52:20,467 --> 00:52:24,167
By the time it's Round Three,
there's nothing left.

1091
00:52:25,197 --> 00:52:26,437
I panicked a bit.

1092
00:52:27,937 --> 00:52:28,937
There aren't many, right?

1093
00:52:29,107 --> 00:52:31,037
There's nothing. They've found everything.

1094
00:52:31,937 --> 00:52:33,807
(The two teams are
focused on calculating.)

1095
00:52:38,217 --> 00:52:40,717
Excuse me, I need one more person
to block with me.

1096
00:52:40,847 --> 00:52:41,847
I'm not curious.

1097
00:52:43,717 --> 00:52:46,427
Nam Hee played a similar role as me.

1098
00:52:46,427 --> 00:52:48,157
She tried to block the view.

1099
00:52:48,247 --> 00:52:50,317
So I wanted to at least stop them...

1100
00:52:50,377 --> 00:52:54,557
from sneaking a peek
to find out about our strategy.

1101
00:52:54,787 --> 00:52:56,157
I defended as best as I could.

1102
00:52:56,487 --> 00:52:58,157
Since this is here...

1103
00:53:06,767 --> 00:53:08,897
Why are you so interested in us?

1104
00:53:09,167 --> 00:53:11,137
- Why are you so interested...
- Don't come close.

1105
00:53:11,137 --> 00:53:12,767
I'm sorry. I didn't mean it.

1106
00:53:12,767 --> 00:53:14,307
- I know, so don't come close.
- I'm sorry.

1107
00:53:14,307 --> 00:53:15,377
You walked toward us.

1108
00:53:15,377 --> 00:53:17,307
- You walked toward us.
- You Hyun keeps getting closer.

1109
00:53:17,377 --> 00:53:18,647
We won't go.

1110
00:53:19,047 --> 00:53:20,547
- I'm just staying here.
- Goodness.

1111
00:53:20,947 --> 00:53:22,117
- Are you okay?
- Are you okay?

1112
00:53:23,247 --> 00:53:24,247
Did they hit you?

1113
00:53:24,387 --> 00:53:25,387
What's wrong?

1114
00:53:25,917 --> 00:53:28,057
- Why are they so violent?
- I'm okay.

1115
00:53:30,417 --> 00:53:31,627
Don't get upset, it's okay.

1116
00:53:32,387 --> 00:53:33,457
They'll go home after this.

1117
00:53:38,397 --> 00:53:39,867
- Did you get pricked?
- I'm okay.

1118
00:53:40,797 --> 00:53:42,037
Let's move to this side.

1119
00:53:42,867 --> 00:53:44,537
Block the view.

1120
00:53:45,067 --> 00:53:47,207
Nam Hee keeps trying to look at ours.

1121
00:53:47,507 --> 00:53:48,537
Gouge out her eyes.

1122
00:53:49,177 --> 00:53:51,247
Nam Hee won't know anything
even if she sees this.

1123
00:53:51,647 --> 00:53:54,477
That team became such an eyesore.

1124
00:53:54,477 --> 00:53:57,987
Honestly, I think You Hyun was
standing diagonally to look at ours.

1125
00:53:58,187 --> 00:54:00,117
We weren't interested in theirs.

1126
00:54:00,287 --> 00:54:01,757
Not interested at all.

1127
00:54:01,957 --> 00:54:04,627
Frankly, I wasn't interested
in their tiles at all.

1128
00:54:04,627 --> 00:54:07,057
Ji Hoo didn't ask us to do much,

1129
00:54:07,327 --> 00:54:08,797
but he said to cover our board
from the other team...

1130
00:54:08,797 --> 00:54:10,257
should they try to see it.

1131
00:54:10,527 --> 00:54:12,867
So I tried to focus on covering the board.

1132
00:54:14,567 --> 00:54:15,997
I'll extend it a bit longer.

1133
00:54:16,537 --> 00:54:18,507
- You're trying to make it longer?
- Yes.

1134
00:54:18,867 --> 00:54:21,277
For us... This is one combination.

1135
00:54:21,737 --> 00:54:23,407
We had 3 pairs of 1 and 9.

1136
00:54:23,737 --> 00:54:26,477
We'd make sum of the tiles in between
become zero...

1137
00:54:26,747 --> 00:54:29,117
and place a plus 9 tile and a plus 1 tile
at the end of each side.

1138
00:54:29,377 --> 00:54:30,847
So it becomes ten.

1139
00:54:31,147 --> 00:54:33,487
These are 1, 2...

1140
00:54:34,287 --> 00:54:37,357
Two, three, four,

1141
00:54:37,357 --> 00:54:38,557
five combinations.

1142
00:54:38,757 --> 00:54:40,287
Next, I'll use 8 and 2.

1143
00:54:40,627 --> 00:54:42,257
Since we have a lot of 8s and 2s. Right.

1144
00:54:43,127 --> 00:54:45,927
(He places the tiles
using the same method.)

1145
00:54:46,527 --> 00:54:47,937
But look here.

1146
00:54:48,137 --> 00:54:49,967
When this combination ends,

1147
00:54:50,037 --> 00:54:51,867
it's better to place another tile
to complete it.

1148
00:54:51,867 --> 00:54:55,437
- Okay.
- I'll start from here and move up.

1149
00:54:55,737 --> 00:54:57,307
And we get another combination.

1150
00:54:57,347 --> 00:54:59,207
Five combinations, ten combinations.

1151
00:54:59,207 --> 00:55:00,717
We have ten combinations now.

1152
00:55:00,917 --> 00:55:02,877
We've already completed ten combinations.

1153
00:55:02,877 --> 00:55:06,087
We could even make up to 30 combinations.

1154
00:55:07,517 --> 00:55:09,687
(Meanwhile, Team Indoor Alliance
has only placed the addition tiles.)

1155
00:55:10,387 --> 00:55:12,587
Will we need to throw away
the tiles at one point?

1156
00:55:13,127 --> 00:55:14,397
Definitely.

1157
00:55:14,697 --> 00:55:16,927
After Round 5 starts,
we have 10 minutes to discard.

1158
00:55:16,927 --> 00:55:18,797
Ten minutes?
That means now is very crucial.

1159
00:55:18,797 --> 00:55:22,337
Yes. We'll see what they find this round,
and he'll make the combinations.

1160
00:55:22,537 --> 00:55:24,037
I'm not disturbing him now.

1161
00:55:24,037 --> 00:55:26,967
If he only makes two combinations,
and only long ones,

1162
00:55:26,967 --> 00:55:29,077
although I doubt it,
then I'll talk to him.

1163
00:55:29,907 --> 00:55:31,077
But he wouldn't do that.

1164
00:55:31,277 --> 00:55:33,807
It's 111.

1165
00:55:36,747 --> 00:55:37,847
And...

1166
00:55:38,317 --> 00:55:41,257
As for what strategy he is using
and what combinations he's forming,

1167
00:55:41,617 --> 00:55:43,357
we were not supposed to get involved.

1168
00:55:43,357 --> 00:55:44,727
Or he'd scold us.

1169
00:55:45,087 --> 00:55:46,957
He was a sensitive student
preparing for his important exam.

1170
00:55:47,397 --> 00:55:49,997
We said we'd trust him and leave it
to him, so we let him be.

1171
00:55:50,727 --> 00:55:53,067
Three minutes until the search ends.

1172
00:55:53,927 --> 00:55:54,967
There's nothing.

1173
00:55:56,137 --> 00:55:57,907
- I found five.
- Really? Good job.

1174
00:55:58,407 --> 00:55:59,437
Let's go quickly.

1175
00:56:06,507 --> 00:56:07,517
Darn it.

1176
00:56:10,217 --> 00:56:11,247
I found a tile too.

1177
00:56:11,247 --> 00:56:12,347
I found one.

1178
00:56:12,517 --> 00:56:13,747
The number isn't important.

1179
00:56:13,747 --> 00:56:16,887
Despite going on a search in Round 3,
I managed to find 1.

1180
00:56:17,057 --> 00:56:20,057
I ran around with much effort.

1181
00:56:20,557 --> 00:56:21,597
Anyway,

1182
00:56:22,227 --> 00:56:23,297
I contributed to the team.

1183
00:56:23,297 --> 00:56:25,367
Team Outdoor Alliance,
will you register your tiles?

1184
00:56:25,367 --> 00:56:26,367
Yes.

1185
00:56:26,527 --> 00:56:29,267
(He also registers the cards
found by Seong Beom.)

1186
00:56:29,567 --> 00:56:31,307
You have found eight tiles in total.

1187
00:56:31,707 --> 00:56:33,567
And can I buy the item now?

1188
00:56:33,767 --> 00:56:36,507
Hong Jin Ho, will you buy a plus ten tile?

1189
00:56:36,507 --> 00:56:37,547
Yes.

1190
00:56:37,577 --> 00:56:39,947
The five tiles have been registered.
Please take them.

1191
00:56:39,947 --> 00:56:41,447
Thank you.

1192
00:56:41,647 --> 00:56:43,217
(Team Outdoor Alliance,
Round 3, Tile Record)

1193
00:56:43,217 --> 00:56:45,647
(Team Outdoor Alliance: 68 tiles)

1194
00:56:45,947 --> 00:56:48,087
Team Indoor Alliance,
will you register the tiles?

1195
00:56:48,087 --> 00:56:49,087
Yes.

1196
00:56:49,187 --> 00:56:50,857
You've found four tiles in total.

1197
00:56:50,857 --> 00:56:53,557
Two tiles have been registered.
Please take them.

1198
00:56:54,027 --> 00:56:55,427
(Team Indoor Alliance,
Round 3, Tile Record)

1199
00:56:55,427 --> 00:56:57,967
(Team Indoor Alliance: 70)

1200
00:56:58,867 --> 00:57:01,167
Let's put this part aside for now.

1201
00:57:01,297 --> 00:57:03,097
- Put it aside for now.
- Hold on.

1202
00:57:03,197 --> 00:57:05,637
Five, six, six.

1203
00:57:05,867 --> 00:57:07,007
Nineteen combinations.

1204
00:57:08,437 --> 00:57:11,107
(Hye Seon is blocking solidly.)

1205
00:57:12,077 --> 00:57:13,147
We're already past 1,000 points.

1206
00:57:13,147 --> 00:57:14,347
It's a nice symmetry.

1207
00:57:14,647 --> 00:57:16,377
More than anything,
our combinations are six-tile long.

1208
00:57:16,817 --> 00:57:18,517
Even with just 20 combinations...

1209
00:57:18,817 --> 00:57:21,257
It's 120 times 20, which is 2,400 points.

1210
00:57:21,617 --> 00:57:23,817
(Team Outdoor Alliance
have already secured 2,400 points.)

1211
00:57:24,087 --> 00:57:25,687
Let's not smile. Darn it.

1212
00:57:26,627 --> 00:57:28,057
What should we do?

1213
00:57:34,737 --> 00:57:35,737
(Meanwhile, Team Indoor Alliance
have simply arranged them.)

1214
00:57:35,737 --> 00:57:38,937
(23 addition tiles, 32 subtraction tiles)

1215
00:57:41,377 --> 00:57:43,607
(Ji Hoo groans)

1216
00:57:43,877 --> 00:57:45,877
Our team having
a lot of subtraction tiles means...

1217
00:57:45,947 --> 00:57:47,747
their team has a lot of addition tiles.

1218
00:57:48,247 --> 00:57:51,547
"We might be at a disadvantage
because we lack addition tiles."

1219
00:57:51,547 --> 00:57:52,687
I was worried about that.

1220
00:57:53,247 --> 00:57:54,257
Okay.

1221
00:57:57,487 --> 00:58:00,127
There's totally nothing left now.

1222
00:58:00,797 --> 00:58:02,697
- Nothing? You couldn't find any?
- Nothing at all.

1223
00:58:02,697 --> 00:58:04,267
- Really? You couldn't find any?
- That's bad. I need more.

1224
00:58:04,267 --> 00:58:05,827
- What should we do?
- I couldn't find a single tile.

1225
00:58:05,827 --> 00:58:06,827
Oh, no.

1226
00:58:06,827 --> 00:58:09,367
(Kwak Beom passes the 4 tiles he's found.)

1227
00:58:09,367 --> 00:58:10,697
(Total number of tiles in Round 3:
23 addition tiles, 32 subtraction tiles)

1228
00:58:10,697 --> 00:58:12,367
- Kwak Beom.
- This much.

1229
00:58:12,367 --> 00:58:14,107
- Good job.
- Two.

1230
00:58:14,107 --> 00:58:15,737
I spent too much time there.

1231
00:58:15,737 --> 00:58:16,877
Good job.

1232
00:58:17,177 --> 00:58:18,947
We kept getting subtraction tiles.

1233
00:58:19,247 --> 00:58:20,747
I got very anxious.

1234
00:58:21,647 --> 00:58:22,777
There barely are any tiles.

1235
00:58:25,617 --> 00:58:27,317
I managed to find one.

1236
00:58:28,087 --> 00:58:29,387
- Eight and...
- Eight.

1237
00:58:29,517 --> 00:58:31,457
- One.
- Eight.

1238
00:58:33,587 --> 00:58:34,597
Oh, it's six.

1239
00:58:37,397 --> 00:58:38,897
Tae Gyun.

1240
00:58:39,097 --> 00:58:40,267
(He finds a plus 1 tile.)

1241
00:58:40,267 --> 00:58:41,497
Hold this.

1242
00:58:41,697 --> 00:58:44,537
Once you form a combination
which you can make a round-trip,

1243
00:58:44,707 --> 00:58:47,537
when you add 1 pair of symmetry,
you get 2 combinations.

1244
00:58:47,877 --> 00:58:51,077
We had four nines and three ones.

1245
00:58:51,147 --> 00:58:54,917
So we had to make the combinations
with three pairs.

1246
00:58:55,017 --> 00:58:58,047
But they found plus one tile,
so we added another pair,

1247
00:58:58,217 --> 00:59:00,447
which gave us additional two combinations.

1248
