01:42:57,487 --> 01:43:00,987
they've earned a total of 5,611 points.

2257
01:43:02,587 --> 01:43:04,657
Today's winners
of the Money Challenge are...

2258
01:43:05,197 --> 01:43:07,627
Team P1 and Team P3.

2259
01:43:17,407 --> 01:43:21,747
The representatives
of Teams P1 and P3, the winners,

2260
01:43:22,007 --> 01:43:23,747
please enter the Voting Room...

2261
01:43:24,117 --> 01:43:26,647
and receive
the 50,000 dollars of team funds.

2262
01:43:28,347 --> 01:43:29,817
I finally get to go in.

2263
01:43:36,287 --> 01:43:37,497
So, this is what it looks like.

2264
01:43:37,927 --> 01:43:40,297
This is the 50,000 dollars,
the prize of the Money Challenge.

2265
01:43:41,397 --> 01:43:44,537
We will store the funds you won
in each team's safe.

2266
01:43:52,707 --> 01:43:56,577
All Deathmatch players,
please gather in the main hall.

2267
01:43:58,147 --> 01:43:59,147
Goodness.

2268
01:44:00,487 --> 01:44:01,847
- What is it?
- What game is this?

2269
01:44:02,287 --> 01:44:03,957
- Why are there only four?
- What's this?

2270
01:44:04,787 --> 01:44:05,817
Why four?

2271
01:44:06,517 --> 01:44:07,887
I think it's 2 against 2.

2272
01:44:08,057 --> 01:44:09,087
Two representatives?

2273
01:44:09,657 --> 01:44:10,697
Two representatives?

2274
01:44:11,097 --> 01:44:12,757
We'll decide
after we find out what the game is.

2275
01:44:13,597 --> 01:44:15,027
There are buzzers.

2276
01:44:16,167 --> 01:44:18,167
I was hoping it'd be a betting game.

2277
01:44:18,467 --> 01:44:19,797
Although Sung Joo is...

2278
01:44:20,737 --> 01:44:22,407
good at betting,

2279
01:44:22,807 --> 01:44:24,437
I think I know...

2280
01:44:24,577 --> 01:44:26,807
his playing style...

2281
01:44:26,807 --> 01:44:29,007
better than he knows my style.

2282
01:44:33,147 --> 01:44:34,187
Team C...

2283
01:44:34,917 --> 01:44:35,987
and Team R...

2284
01:44:36,647 --> 01:44:40,527
will have a team Deathmatch.

2285
01:44:41,527 --> 01:44:43,387
All members of the losing team...

2286
01:44:43,997 --> 01:44:45,757
will be eliminated.

2287
01:44:47,227 --> 01:44:51,797
Now, I will announce today's Deathmatch.

2288
01:44:53,137 --> 01:44:54,567
Today's Deathmatch is...

2289
01:44:55,207 --> 01:44:57,037
(Ring the Bell)

2290
01:44:57,037 --> 01:44:59,437
Ring the Bell.

2291
01:45:01,007 --> 01:45:03,447
Ring the Bell is a card game
where players swap cards...

2292
01:45:03,677 --> 01:45:05,647
to form higher-ranking combinations...

2293
01:45:06,247 --> 01:45:07,987
and ring the bell at the optimal moment...

2294
01:45:08,287 --> 01:45:11,717
to resolve their hands.

2295
01:45:12,357 --> 01:45:13,387
Gosh.

2296
01:45:14,757 --> 01:45:17,157
Each round features four players,

2297
01:45:17,457 --> 01:45:19,497
two from each team,

2298
01:45:19,827 --> 01:45:22,697
and every team member must participate...

2299
01:45:22,927 --> 01:45:25,297
at least once across the first two rounds.

2300
01:45:26,597 --> 01:45:29,707
A single round consists
of up to nine sets.

2301
01:45:30,277 --> 01:45:31,577
At the start of each set,

2302
01:45:31,677 --> 01:45:34,277
a 40-card deck,
comprising 4 colors numbered 1 through 10,

2303
01:45:34,547 --> 01:45:36,547
is shuffled,

2304
01:45:37,147 --> 01:45:40,147
and each player is dealt four cards.

2305
01:45:41,187 --> 01:45:44,587
The remaining cards form
a face-down draw pile,

2306
01:45:45,087 --> 01:45:47,757
with the top card flipped face-up.

2307
01:45:48,457 --> 01:45:52,027
On your turn,
you must perform 1 of 2 actions.

2308
01:45:52,397 --> 01:45:54,597
One, swap a card.

2309
01:45:54,927 --> 01:45:56,297
Draw one card...

2310
01:45:56,397 --> 01:45:58,767
from either the face-down pile
or the face-up card,

2311
01:45:59,337 --> 01:46:01,667
then discard one card from your hand.

2312
01:46:02,267 --> 01:46:05,607
You can immediately discard
the card you just drew.

2313
01:46:05,807 --> 01:46:09,577
The discarded card becomes
the new face-up card for the next player.

2314
01:46:10,107 --> 01:46:12,177
Two, ring the bell.

2315
01:46:12,517 --> 01:46:13,947
When a player rings the bell,

2316
01:46:14,187 --> 01:46:16,917
all other players get one final turn...

2317
01:46:17,257 --> 01:46:20,217
to swap a card in order.

2318
01:46:20,827 --> 01:46:22,227
Once the turn returns...

2319
01:46:22,227 --> 01:46:24,557
to the player who rang the bell,

2320
01:46:24,897 --> 01:46:26,897
everyone reveals...

2321
01:46:26,897 --> 01:46:28,967
their card combination,
starting with that player.

2322
01:46:30,097 --> 01:46:32,997
A combination can consist...

2323
01:46:32,997 --> 01:46:35,137
of 1 to 4 cards.

2324
01:46:35,467 --> 01:46:37,577
However, if you combine two or more cards,

2325
01:46:38,037 --> 01:46:40,137
they must all share
either the same number...

2326
01:46:40,277 --> 01:46:42,547
or the same color.

2327
01:46:43,977 --> 01:46:46,317
After all hands are revealed,

2328
01:46:46,477 --> 01:46:48,047
the sum of the numbers
in each combination is compared.

2329
01:46:48,287 --> 01:46:50,317
The player with the lowest sum...

2330
01:46:50,417 --> 01:46:52,817
loses one Life.

2331
01:46:53,687 --> 01:46:57,057
If multiple players tie
for the lowest sum,

2332
01:46:57,457 --> 01:47:00,467
all tied players lose one Life.

2333
01:47:00,997 --> 01:47:04,497
Additionally, if the player
who rang the bell has the lowest sum,

2334
01:47:04,967 --> 01:47:08,507
they lose one extra Life as a penalty.

2335
01:47:09,407 --> 01:47:12,907
If you collect four cards
of the same number on your turn,

2336
01:47:13,437 --> 01:47:17,117
you can declare a "Four of a Kind"
and ring the bell immediately.

2337
01:47:18,377 --> 01:47:20,647
In this case,
no card comparison takes place,

2338
01:47:21,287 --> 01:47:25,187
and both players on the opposing team
automatically lose one Life.

2339
01:47:26,017 --> 01:47:29,287
However, once another player
has already rung the bell,

2340
01:47:29,557 --> 01:47:31,657
a "Four of a Kind" declaration
can no longer be made,

2341
01:47:31,857 --> 01:47:34,897
and the set proceeds
to standard combination comparison.

2342
01:47:35,867 --> 01:47:38,697
If the face-down draw pile runs out,

2343
01:47:39,097 --> 01:47:41,737
all players must immediately reveal
their combinations in turn order.

2344
01:47:42,267 --> 01:47:43,607
When a set ends,

2345
01:47:43,837 --> 01:47:47,007
if any player loses all three Life points,

2346
01:47:47,547 --> 01:47:49,807
that player's team loses,

2347
01:47:49,807 --> 01:47:51,447
and the round immediately ends.

2348
01:47:52,577 --> 01:47:56,787
If players from both teams lose
their final Life simultaneously,

2349
01:47:56,917 --> 01:48:00,657
the team of the player who rang the bell
in that final set wins the round.

2350
01:48:01,827 --> 01:48:03,897
The game is played
over a maximum of three rounds,

2351
01:48:04,497 --> 01:48:06,497
and the first team to win two rounds...

2352
01:48:06,697 --> 01:48:08,627
will be the surviving team
of the Deathmatch.

2353
01:48:09,697 --> 01:48:12,867
Ring the Bell will begin shortly.

2354
01:48:13,737 --> 01:48:15,807
It's my type of game.

2355
01:48:15,907 --> 01:48:18,977
I'm pretty confident
I can come up with a good strategy...

2356
01:48:18,977 --> 01:48:20,877
in a game like this.

2357
01:48:21,147 --> 01:48:23,547
Winning isn't important here.
You only have to avoid placing last.

2358
01:48:23,747 --> 01:48:26,447
If there's a 50-percent chance
or higher...

2359
01:48:26,777 --> 01:48:30,317
that we don't have the lowest sum,
we're going to ring the bell.

2360
01:48:30,557 --> 01:48:32,657
Sung Joo and I are poker players,

2361
01:48:32,657 --> 01:48:34,927
and I must keep him in check.

2362
01:48:35,057 --> 01:48:37,127
But I was pretty confident in this game.

2363
01:48:37,127 --> 01:48:39,757
Also, Team R doesn't look so strong.

2364
01:48:40,397 --> 01:48:41,527
You Hyun is...

2365
01:48:41,667 --> 01:48:45,397
well-balanced in most games.

2366
01:48:45,497 --> 01:48:46,797
He has various good qualities.

2367
01:48:47,097 --> 01:48:49,367
But I didn't think we really fell behind.

2368
01:48:50,537 --> 01:48:52,107
It requires a good sense of numbers.

2369
01:48:52,107 --> 01:48:53,907
Four players are in this game,

2370
01:48:53,907 --> 01:48:56,007
so you need to know
when you think you'll win.

2371
01:48:56,177 --> 01:48:58,777
You must compare
the most accurate guesses...

2372
01:48:58,777 --> 01:49:00,377
of their numbers...

2373
01:49:00,687 --> 01:49:02,717
and ring the bell...

2374
01:49:02,717 --> 01:49:04,657
when you're a number,
or even half a number ahead of others.

2375
01:49:05,257 --> 01:49:06,487
This is poker.

2376
01:49:06,887 --> 01:49:08,887
You Hyun and Sung Joo,

2377
01:49:08,887 --> 01:49:11,727
the poker players, will be great at this.

2378
01:49:11,957 --> 01:49:15,597
I plan on figuring out
at what sum you should ring the bell.

2379
01:49:15,727 --> 01:49:18,237
I'm going to calculate
the possibilities...

2380
01:49:18,237 --> 01:49:21,407
and tell them
when they should ring the bell.

2381
01:49:21,867 --> 01:49:25,377
I felt that you could win
by not having the lowest sum...

2382
01:49:25,507 --> 01:49:28,607
rather than by having the highest sum.

2383
01:49:28,777 --> 01:49:31,077
I haven't played that many card games,

2384
01:49:31,077 --> 01:49:34,617
so I wasn't that confident.

2385
01:49:35,147 --> 01:49:37,417
You have ten minutes
to confer with your team...

2386
01:49:37,987 --> 01:49:41,127
and finalize the rosters
for Rounds 1 and 2.

2387
01:49:42,787 --> 01:49:43,857
- Come on over.
- Okay.

2388
01:49:44,027 --> 01:49:46,157
I'll tell you the basic principles.

2389
01:49:47,367 --> 01:49:48,697
It's called Ring the Bell...

2390
01:49:49,127 --> 01:49:50,197
because you're supposed
to ring the bell...

2391
01:49:50,197 --> 01:49:52,167
when you have a high sum
and the opponents have low sums.

2392
01:49:52,537 --> 01:49:55,107
To tell each other our average sums,

2393
01:49:55,107 --> 01:49:57,377
we need to come up with hand signals.

2394
01:49:57,507 --> 01:49:59,607
We have to decide.

2395
01:49:59,937 --> 01:50:01,107
I think...

2396
01:50:01,307 --> 01:50:04,217
the signal to tell each other
whether to ring it or not matters most.

2397
01:50:04,377 --> 01:50:07,447
It shouldn't be a signal
that we might do by mistake.

2398
01:50:07,617 --> 01:50:08,687
For instance...

2399
01:50:09,717 --> 01:50:12,917
If you're touching the table,

2400
01:50:13,117 --> 01:50:15,187
it means you're ready. Okay?

2401
01:50:15,757 --> 01:50:19,157
When we both have
a 50-percent chance or higher...

2402
01:50:19,157 --> 01:50:20,797
to win the set...

2403
01:50:20,797 --> 01:50:23,267
and we're touching the table,

2404
01:50:23,567 --> 01:50:25,897
we're going to ring the bell.

2405
01:50:26,037 --> 01:50:27,507
That was our strategy.

2406
01:50:27,967 --> 01:50:30,407
And I should tell you this.
They must be the same color.

2407
01:50:30,507 --> 01:50:32,477
- Right.
- Don't even go for Four of a Kind.

2408
01:50:32,577 --> 01:50:34,107
Try not to make that combination.

2409
01:50:34,107 --> 01:50:35,647
- It's practically zero.
- It is.

2410
01:50:35,877 --> 01:50:38,447
But if I get three fours,

2411
01:50:38,817 --> 01:50:41,217
am I supposed to create
a same-color combination?

2412
01:50:41,217 --> 01:50:42,347
- Yes.
- Yes.

2413
01:50:42,547 --> 01:50:43,647
- Okay?
- Okay.

2414
01:50:43,787 --> 01:50:46,517
If we have one card each,
the average is...

2415
01:50:47,117 --> 01:50:48,387
Is it 5.5?

2416
01:50:48,987 --> 01:50:51,857
But it's not likely
to win with only one card.

2417
01:50:51,897 --> 01:50:53,127
- Statistically.
- Exactly.

2418
01:50:53,127 --> 01:50:54,497
I bet it's two at best.

2419
01:50:54,497 --> 01:50:55,867
- Two of the same color.
- Yes.

2420
01:50:56,097 --> 01:50:57,567
So, 5.5 is the average.

2421
01:50:57,737 --> 01:50:59,967
When it's 2 cards, the total should be 11.

2422
01:51:00,667 --> 01:51:02,637
I think the standard should be 11.

2423
01:51:02,637 --> 01:51:03,737
- You're right.
- Yes.

2424
01:51:04,537 --> 01:51:06,837
The cards are 1 through 10,
so the average...

2425
01:51:06,837 --> 01:51:08,007
is 5.5.

2426
01:51:08,007 --> 01:51:09,607
We get four cards at first,

2427
01:51:09,847 --> 01:51:12,617
we're most likely to have
two cards of the same color.

2428
01:51:12,977 --> 01:51:15,047
The average sum of two cards
of the same color...

2429
01:51:15,387 --> 01:51:18,117
is 5.5 times 2, so it's 11.

2430
01:51:18,587 --> 01:51:20,087
When we first receive four cards,

2431
01:51:20,827 --> 01:51:23,427
and if the sum of the same color is
11 or higher,

2432
01:51:24,597 --> 01:51:25,827
that means you're in the top 50 percent.

2433
01:51:26,227 --> 01:51:28,297
Setting 11 as the standard is...

2434
01:51:28,997 --> 01:51:32,137
only when the opposing team
hasn't swapped any cards.

2435
01:51:32,267 --> 01:51:34,037
- Yes, we're talking about the first turn.
- Yes, the very first turn.

2436
01:51:34,037 --> 01:51:36,367
Say you're going first,

2437
01:51:36,507 --> 01:51:37,607
and both teammates are touching the table,

2438
01:51:37,607 --> 01:51:39,737
that means they're both 11 or higher.
Then, you ring the bell.

2439
01:51:40,077 --> 01:51:42,947
If you swapped the cards
and the other guy also did,

2440
01:51:43,207 --> 01:51:44,617
we have to raise the standard.

2441
01:51:44,617 --> 01:51:46,317
The sum exponentially increases...

2442
01:51:46,317 --> 01:51:48,047
after each turn.

2443
01:51:48,047 --> 01:51:49,987
Because they can randomly draw...

2444
01:51:49,987 --> 01:51:52,287
the same number or the same color.

2445
01:51:52,657 --> 01:51:54,857
This is an estimate,

2446
01:51:55,287 --> 01:51:57,397
but I think it's 11, 14, 17,

2447
01:51:58,257 --> 01:51:59,757
- and 19.
- Okay.

2448
01:51:59,927 --> 01:52:01,397
All right. Here's what we're doing.

2449
01:52:01,797 --> 01:52:03,397
No one has swapped any cards yet,

2450
01:52:03,397 --> 01:52:05,137
then 11 is your go sign.

2451
01:52:05,297 --> 01:52:07,237
- If you've swapped a card once,
- Yes.

2452
01:52:07,237 --> 01:52:08,937
then 14 is your go sign.

2453
01:52:09,137 --> 01:52:10,907
- And if you've swapped two cards,
- Yes.

2454
01:52:10,907 --> 01:52:12,437
- then 17 is your go sign.
- Okay.

2455
01:52:12,837 --> 01:52:15,107
If either of your hands is
touching the table,

2456
01:52:15,777 --> 01:52:19,447
it means your hand is above that value.

2457
01:52:19,447 --> 01:52:20,517
- Yes.
- Okay.

2458
01:52:20,947 --> 01:52:22,287
But once you ring the bell,

2459
01:52:22,287 --> 01:52:23,817
the other three swap cards.

2460
01:52:24,087 --> 01:52:25,287
- You're right.
- Yes.

2461
01:52:25,387 --> 01:52:26,957
The one who rings the bell...

2462
01:52:27,257 --> 01:52:28,887
- must have 14 or higher.
- Right.

2463
01:52:29,527 --> 01:52:31,927
I made some predictions...

2464
01:52:32,057 --> 01:52:33,327
using my mathematical intuition.

2465
01:52:33,327 --> 01:52:35,197
So, they're 11, 14, 17,

2466
01:52:35,967 --> 01:52:37,467
then 19 and 21.

2467
01:52:37,737 --> 01:52:39,637
And then, it can't go that high,

2468
01:52:39,797 --> 01:52:41,337
so they're 22, 23, and 24.

2469
01:52:41,567 --> 01:52:44,537
The one who rings the bell misses a turn,

2470
01:52:44,837 --> 01:52:46,377
so the average should be much higher.

2471
01:52:46,377 --> 01:52:49,677
If the average sum of that round is 14,

2472
01:52:50,177 --> 01:52:52,077
the average sum of the next round is 17,

2473
01:52:52,447 --> 01:52:55,517
so the one who rings the bell must have
the sum of 17 or higher.

2474
01:52:55,547 --> 01:52:57,557
And their teammate...

2475
01:52:57,557 --> 01:52:58,917
can only have 14.

2476
01:52:59,287 --> 01:53:01,587
That was our strategy.

2477
01:53:01,887 --> 01:53:05,127
This should be confusing.

2478
01:53:05,297 --> 01:53:07,197
It's all right.
Let me break it down for you.

2479
01:53:07,767 --> 01:53:09,927
The very first hand before any swaps.

2480
01:53:10,097 --> 01:53:11,267
- It's 11.
- It is.

2481
01:53:11,267 --> 01:53:12,597
But if you want to ring the bell,

2482
01:53:12,867 --> 01:53:15,607
you think what the next average sum is.

2483
01:53:16,067 --> 01:53:17,707
- So, it's 14.
- But if you don't want to,

2484
01:53:17,707 --> 01:53:19,607
your go sign is still 11.

2485
01:53:19,937 --> 01:53:21,247
And once you touch a card,

2486
01:53:21,247 --> 01:53:22,947
you level up.

2487
01:53:23,147 --> 01:53:24,217
Then, your go sign is 14.

2488
01:53:24,217 --> 01:53:25,477
Yes. And if you want to ring the bell,

2489
01:53:25,477 --> 01:53:27,847
- then you think about what's next.
- That's 17.

2490
01:53:28,117 --> 01:53:29,517
That means your sum must be
higher than 17.

2491
01:53:30,417 --> 01:53:32,157
Tell me if I understood correctly.

2492
01:53:32,387 --> 01:53:35,127
If I'm the one ringing the bell,
it starts from 14.

2493
01:53:35,127 --> 01:53:38,057
It goes 14, 17, 19, and 21.

2494
01:53:38,297 --> 01:53:39,757
But if I'm...

2495
01:53:39,757 --> 01:53:42,267
supposed to touch the table,
it starts from 11.

2496
01:53:42,267 --> 01:53:44,897
It's 11, 14, 17, 19, and 21.

2497
01:53:44,897 --> 01:53:46,367
- Is that the right sequence?
- Yes.

2498
01:53:46,367 --> 01:53:47,367
- Okay.
- Okay.

2499
01:53:47,367 --> 01:53:48,707
It's easier to memorize that way.

2500
01:53:49,037 --> 01:53:50,267
(Team C's strategy)

2501
01:53:50,267 --> 01:53:51,807
(0 swaps: 11, 1 swap: 14,
2 swaps: 17, 3 swaps: 19, 4 swaps: 21)

2502
01:53:51,807 --> 01:53:53,307
(After that,
it increases by 1 every swap.)

2503
01:53:53,307 --> 01:53:58,747
(But the one ringing the bell must have
the sum of the higher swap.)

2504
01:53:58,747 --> 01:54:00,847
Getting Four of a Kind is...

2505
01:54:01,387 --> 01:54:02,987
It's practically impossible
unless you're incredibly lucky.

2506
01:54:02,987 --> 01:54:04,687
- We should go with the same color.
- Yes.

2507
01:54:05,217 --> 01:54:06,887
- High cards of the same color.
- Yes.

2508
01:54:07,087 --> 01:54:08,327
It has to be.

2509
01:54:08,527 --> 01:54:09,827
Four of a Kind is out of the question.

2510
01:54:09,927 --> 01:54:11,457
You'd have to be a fool to aim for that.

2511
01:54:11,527 --> 01:54:13,727
That's something that will never happen.

2512
01:54:13,727 --> 01:54:17,467
Just because you have three fours,

2513
01:54:17,467 --> 01:54:20,037
discarding the card the whole time...

2514
01:54:20,037 --> 01:54:21,107
only to have the sum of 12...

2515
01:54:21,107 --> 01:54:22,507
is unacceptable.

2516
01:54:22,967 --> 01:54:25,137
I think the signals are crucial.

2517
01:54:25,377 --> 01:54:27,547
The signal between the two
to say you're ringing the bell.

2518
01:54:27,977 --> 01:54:29,247
If we both have good hands,

2519
01:54:29,447 --> 01:54:30,977
and the opposing team
doesn't ring the bell,

2520
01:54:30,977 --> 01:54:33,047
we need something to tell each other.

2521
01:54:33,047 --> 01:54:34,287
- Yes.
- Yes.

2522
01:54:34,287 --> 01:54:36,387
Let's say I have the sum...

2523
01:54:36,387 --> 01:54:37,917
- of 20 or 21.
- Okay.

2524
01:54:38,387 --> 01:54:41,187
Then, I want my opponents to believe
that I was dealt a bad hand.

2525
01:54:41,387 --> 01:54:44,327
I'm going to draw a card from the pile
and pass as if I have a bad hand,

2526
01:54:44,327 --> 01:54:46,627
and the opposing team might ring the bell.

2527
01:54:46,897 --> 01:54:48,727
Then, we're never going to ring the bell.

2528
01:54:49,597 --> 01:54:50,797
Because we'll lose two Life points.

2529
01:54:51,537 --> 01:54:54,367
When our sum is 20 or higher,
we're going to bluff.

2530
01:54:54,467 --> 01:54:57,207
It's such a safe number,
so the other team loses two Life points...

2531
01:54:57,907 --> 01:54:59,207
if they ring the bell.

2532
01:54:59,507 --> 01:55:00,707
Let's do it this way.

2533
01:55:01,447 --> 01:55:02,907
A hand signal for a go sign...

2534
01:55:03,307 --> 01:55:04,477
and another for a bluff.

2535
01:55:04,477 --> 01:55:06,317
You'll feel it
when you want to ring the bell.

2536
01:55:06,317 --> 01:55:07,317
- Yes, that's all we need.
- Yes.

2537
01:55:07,317 --> 01:55:09,017
So, you tell your teammate that.

2538
01:55:09,387 --> 01:55:11,487
And the numbers
we think are safe to go for it.

2539
01:55:11,487 --> 01:55:13,617
We should set them beforehand
whether it's 16 or 17.

2540
01:55:13,617 --> 01:55:16,487
I'd say it's 16 or 17 on average.

2541
01:55:16,487 --> 01:55:17,557
Okay.

2542
01:55:17,557 --> 01:55:19,627
Let's set it at 16.

2543
01:55:19,627 --> 01:55:22,967
But you send a signal...

2544
01:55:23,497 --> 01:55:27,067
only when you've checked your hand...

2545
01:55:27,267 --> 01:55:29,267
- after a swap.
- Right.

2546
01:55:31,137 --> 01:55:33,637
- What should be our signal?
- Let's touch our ears.

2547
01:55:33,637 --> 01:55:36,077
You touch your nose and everything,

2548
01:55:36,077 --> 01:55:38,347
but we only care about the ears. Okay?

2549
01:55:39,017 --> 01:55:41,087
It's the same system
as the one used for signs in baseball.

2550
01:55:41,447 --> 01:55:42,987
Keep doing things to distract them.

2551
01:55:43,217 --> 01:55:44,357
Confuse them.

2552
01:55:44,357 --> 01:55:46,357
But what matters is our ears.

2553
01:55:46,487 --> 01:55:47,657
The ear is the go sign.

2554
01:55:47,657 --> 01:55:49,087
That's the go sign.

2555
01:55:49,257 --> 01:55:50,587
What should be our bluff sign?

2556
01:55:51,197 --> 01:55:54,927
You bluff when you touch the Adam's apple.

2557
01:55:55,667 --> 01:55:56,967
I don't think it's that bad.

2558
01:55:59,137 --> 01:56:01,967
How long are we going to bluff
when our sum is 20?

2559
01:56:02,237 --> 01:56:03,537
How many turns are we dragging it out?

2560
01:56:03,737 --> 01:56:07,107
Say we got 20 in the first 2 turns.

2561
01:56:07,307 --> 01:56:09,177
Then, we bluff.

2562
01:56:09,277 --> 01:56:10,647
But we ring the bell on the third turn.

2563
01:56:10,807 --> 01:56:12,217
If we're going to bluff,

2564
01:56:12,217 --> 01:56:15,017
we both need to get the sum of 20
in the first 2 turns.

2565
01:56:15,017 --> 01:56:16,017
Yes.

2566
01:56:16,047 --> 01:56:18,357
We could be in that situation
by coincidence.

2567
01:56:18,987 --> 01:56:20,717
But we might not win on the third turn,

2568
01:56:20,717 --> 01:56:22,387
- so we ring the bell.
- Okay.

2569
01:56:22,387 --> 01:56:23,557
- We stop bluffing?
- Yes.

2570
01:56:23,557 --> 01:56:24,557
- Okay.
- Okay.

2571
01:56:24,557 --> 01:56:26,927
Remember the go sign and the bluff sign.

2572
01:56:27,057 --> 01:56:28,397
Tell me what it is. What's the go sign?

2573
01:56:28,897 --> 01:56:30,167
- This is the go sign.
- Yes.

2574
01:56:30,497 --> 01:56:32,497
- And this is the bluff sign.
- Yes.

2575
01:56:32,497 --> 01:56:33,567
Okay.

2576
01:56:33,567 --> 01:56:35,407
But you have to touch your nose
and everything too.

2577
01:56:35,567 --> 01:56:36,867
- Mix it up.
- Yes.

2578
01:56:36,867 --> 01:56:38,277
(Team R's strategy)

2579
01:56:38,277 --> 01:56:39,837
(Hand signals)

2580
01:56:39,837 --> 01:56:41,477
(Touch your ear
when your sum is 16 or higher.)

2581
01:56:41,477 --> 01:56:43,107
(Touch your Adam's apple
when your sum is 20 or higher to bluff.)

2582
01:56:43,107 --> 01:56:44,717
(But you only bluff for 2 turns.
You ring the bell on the 3rd turn.)

2583
01:56:45,047 --> 01:56:47,177
But we have to submit the roster
of the first two rounds.

2584
01:56:47,517 --> 01:56:48,947
You two should play in Round One.

2585
01:56:49,547 --> 01:56:50,787
We need the roster for Round Two.

2586
01:56:50,787 --> 01:56:52,417
- Why don't you and I go?
- Okay.

2587
01:56:53,487 --> 01:56:56,857
Seung Yong and Sung Joo,
who actively came up with the plan,

2588
01:56:56,857 --> 01:56:59,097
will play first.
Sung Joo is a poker player, after all.

2589
01:56:59,497 --> 01:57:00,827
Those two go first,

2590
01:57:00,827 --> 01:57:03,067
Then, a poker player...

2591
01:57:03,467 --> 01:57:04,897
and I play next.

2592
01:57:05,567 --> 01:57:08,407
I think it all comes down
to the poker players' strategies.

2593
01:57:09,067 --> 01:57:11,407
You Hyun's card strategy...

2594
01:57:11,837 --> 01:57:15,747
versus Sung Joo's poker strategy.

2595
01:57:16,377 --> 01:57:17,877
Should we pair up?

2596
01:57:18,217 --> 01:57:19,977
That way, one of us can tell the other.

2597
01:57:19,977 --> 01:57:22,587
All you do is ring the bell
and swap the cards.

2598
01:57:22,587 --> 01:57:23,587
Nam Hee and I will play in Round One,

2599
01:57:23,587 --> 01:57:24,617
- Okay.
- so you can go next.

2600
01:57:24,617 --> 01:57:26,157
- Nam Hee, are you sure you understand?
- Yes.

2601
01:57:26,157 --> 01:57:27,457
- Yes, she understood.
- Good.

2602
01:57:27,757 --> 01:57:29,987
The strategy meeting session is over.

2603
01:57:30,997 --> 01:57:33,327
Please submit your lineup
in the order of participation.

2604
01:57:37,167 --> 01:57:39,967
(Round 1: You Hyun and Nam Hee
versus Sung Joo and Seung Yong)

2605
01:57:39,967 --> 01:57:42,537
(Round 2: Kyoung Hoon and Ji Hoo
versus Sung Joo and Beom)

2606
01:57:43,167 --> 01:57:44,877
Seat assignments
and the starting player...

2607
01:57:44,877 --> 01:57:46,437
will be determined by drawing cards.

2608
01:57:46,437 --> 01:57:47,577
Nam Hee, you can draw it.

2609
01:57:49,347 --> 01:57:51,817
The player who draws number 1
will take positions 1 and 3,

2610
01:57:53,147 --> 01:57:56,287
and the player who draws number 2
will take positions 2 and 4.

2611
01:57:58,617 --> 01:57:59,787
(Team R drew number 2.)

2612
01:58:00,187 --> 01:58:01,227
Team C...

2613
01:58:01,987 --> 01:58:03,857
has drawn card number one.

2614
01:58:03,927 --> 01:58:09,097
(Round 1 order: You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, and Seung Yong)

2615
01:58:09,927 --> 01:58:11,667
Round One will begin now.

2616
01:58:12,797 --> 01:58:15,367
- I think they started.
- Did they?

2617
01:58:15,367 --> 01:58:16,367
Yes.

2618
01:58:16,567 --> 01:58:19,377
We will now begin the 1st set of Round 1.

2619
01:58:20,107 --> 01:58:22,547
(Team C, Kim You Hyun)

2620
01:58:22,647 --> 01:58:25,017
(Team R, Hyun Sung Joo)

2621
01:58:25,747 --> 01:58:27,577
(Team C, Kim Nam Hee)

2622
01:58:28,187 --> 01:58:30,087
(Team R, Shin Seung Yong)

2623
01:58:48,837 --> 01:58:49,967
What's that?

2624
01:58:50,107 --> 01:58:53,337
It's what poker players do
to protect their cards.

2625
01:58:53,407 --> 01:58:55,577
He and I are the only ones doing it.

2626
01:58:57,677 --> 01:58:59,347
Even when playing poker,

2627
01:58:59,347 --> 01:59:01,487
You Hyun's raw hardware,
his brain, is just that good.

2628
01:59:02,147 --> 01:59:03,287
I made up my mind to stay sharp.

2629
01:59:03,917 --> 01:59:06,987
I was confident I could defeat Sung Joo
in a Deathmatch.

2630
01:59:17,397 --> 01:59:19,297
Please check the open card.

2631
01:59:22,067 --> 01:59:23,067
My neck hurts.

2632
01:59:23,067 --> 01:59:25,307
You Hyun, please begin your turn.

2633
01:59:25,407 --> 01:59:28,477
(You Hyun)

2634
01:59:28,477 --> 01:59:30,577
The one ringing the bell must have
the sum of 14 or higher,

2635
01:59:30,677 --> 01:59:32,677
and the other one's sum
only has to be above 11.

2636
01:59:33,047 --> 01:59:34,687
But Nam Hee wasn't giving me a sign.

2637
01:59:36,317 --> 01:59:38,157
(Team C promised to lean on the table...)

2638
01:59:38,157 --> 01:59:41,627
(once they had the sum
that was high enough.)

2639
01:59:42,457 --> 01:59:44,257
(But Nam Hee is standing
far from the table.)

2640
01:59:44,257 --> 01:59:45,757
And my sum wasn't higher than 14.

2641
01:59:46,557 --> 01:59:47,797
I'll get one from the pile.

2642
01:59:48,327 --> 01:59:50,027
You've chosen the face-down card.

2643
01:59:50,027 --> 01:59:51,137
(You Hyun: 12, face-up card: 6)

2644
01:59:51,137 --> 01:59:53,267
(You Hyun: 12)

2645
01:59:53,267 --> 01:59:55,667
You've discarded card one in yellow.

2646
01:59:56,037 --> 01:59:57,877
Sung Joo, it's your turn.

2647
01:59:58,177 --> 02:00:01,007
(Sung Joo: 8, face-up card: 1)

2648
02:00:01,007 --> 02:00:02,147
I'll take one from the pile.

2649
02:00:02,147 --> 02:00:04,747
(Sung Joo: 8, face-up card: 1)

2650
02:00:13,557 --> 02:00:16,257
My two cards in blue were low,
so I was going to discard them.

2651
02:00:17,357 --> 02:00:20,457
It was a no-brainer
to make the combination...

2652
02:00:20,697 --> 02:00:21,997
of 16 or higher.

2653
02:00:23,797 --> 02:00:26,097
You've discarded card two in blue.

2654
02:00:26,297 --> 02:00:28,037
I gave up card two in blue at first.

2655
02:00:29,407 --> 02:00:31,307
Nam Hee, it's your turn.

2656
02:00:31,307 --> 02:00:32,377
The pile.

2657
02:00:32,607 --> 02:00:34,377
You've chosen a face-down card.

2658
02:00:34,377 --> 02:00:35,377
(Nam Hee: 11, face-up card: 2)

2659
02:00:36,047 --> 02:00:37,577
Oh, my heart.

2660
02:00:38,347 --> 02:00:40,377
I feel like it's beating
three times at once.

2661
02:00:44,687 --> 02:00:46,917
I didn't know
what the next number would be,

2662
02:00:47,057 --> 02:00:49,927
so I couldn't decide whether to keep
two pairs of the same color or...

2663
02:00:50,827 --> 02:00:51,997
Gosh.

2664
02:00:53,197 --> 02:00:54,667
Should I throw this away?

2665
02:00:57,227 --> 02:00:59,567
You've discarded card nine in red.

2666
02:01:00,237 --> 02:01:01,407
Are you bluffing?

2667
02:01:03,567 --> 02:01:04,737
(Face-up card: 9)

2668
02:01:04,737 --> 02:01:07,337
I don't know what cards she holds,

2669
02:01:07,337 --> 02:01:10,107
so I wondered why she had to
discard a number nine card.

2670
02:01:10,107 --> 02:01:11,217
Did she have 3 cards with number 10?

2671
02:01:11,217 --> 02:01:12,617
Is her sum 30 already?

2672
02:01:12,617 --> 02:01:15,087
It made me wonder why.

2673
02:01:15,387 --> 02:01:16,587
She must have a strong hand.

2674
02:01:19,557 --> 02:01:20,617
Nam Hee, you remember, right?

2675
02:01:21,487 --> 02:01:22,957
Right? You remember this, right?

2676
02:01:26,397 --> 02:01:28,897
I was really nervous at first.

2677
02:01:29,497 --> 02:01:31,767
I had a number 11 card at first,

2678
02:01:31,997 --> 02:01:33,367
but I couldn't stick to the strategy.

2679
02:01:34,767 --> 02:01:36,607
If we had a sum bigger than 11,

2680
02:01:36,607 --> 02:01:38,277
we were supposed to
give each other a signal.

2681
02:01:38,277 --> 02:01:40,237
The signal was sticking my body
onto the table.

2682
02:01:40,237 --> 02:01:42,347
But I failed to do that...

2683
02:01:42,577 --> 02:01:44,447
when I was holding cards
with numbers bigger than 11.

2684
02:01:45,777 --> 02:01:47,847
Seung Yong, it's your turn.

2685
02:01:50,717 --> 02:01:52,957
(Seung Yong touches his Adam's apple
right away.)

2686
02:01:56,627 --> 02:01:59,097
(The signal was touching ears
when the number is higher than 16...)

2687
02:01:59,097 --> 02:02:01,597
(and Adam's apple
when the number is higher than 20.)

2688
02:02:01,697 --> 02:02:04,067
(Shin Seung Yong)

2689
02:02:07,237 --> 02:02:08,307
I'll take the back card.

2690
02:02:08,537 --> 02:02:10,467
The back card has been selected.

2691
02:02:10,467 --> 02:02:12,577
(Shin Seung Yong)

2692
02:02:18,677 --> 02:02:21,017
You've discarded card six in blue.

2693
02:02:21,017 --> 02:02:23,017
(Shin Seung Yong)

2694
02:02:23,247 --> 02:02:25,757
Seung Yong was ready,

2695
02:02:25,757 --> 02:02:27,317
but I wasn't.

2696
02:02:27,317 --> 02:02:29,587
You Hyun, it's your turn.

2697
02:02:29,587 --> 02:02:33,627
(Front card: 6, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2698
02:02:33,627 --> 02:02:34,697
I'll take card number six.

2699
02:02:34,897 --> 02:02:36,897
You've chosen card six in blue.

2700
02:02:36,897 --> 02:02:38,897
(Front card: 6, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2701
02:02:38,897 --> 02:02:40,937
You've discarded card three in yellow.

2702
02:02:40,937 --> 02:02:43,907
(Front card: 3, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2703
02:02:47,237 --> 02:02:50,077
You Hyun had a sum higher than 17,

2704
02:02:50,077 --> 02:02:51,247
so he kept leaning on the table.

2705
02:02:52,317 --> 02:02:54,687
Sung Joo, it's your turn.

2706
02:02:54,687 --> 02:02:58,217
(Front card: 3, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2707
02:02:58,217 --> 02:02:59,217
I'll take a back card.

2708
02:02:59,217 --> 02:03:01,187
The back card has been selected.

2709
02:03:01,187 --> 02:03:04,257
(Front card: 3, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2710
02:03:06,397 --> 02:03:08,027
Since I had 2 cards of 6,

2711
02:03:08,027 --> 02:03:11,337
I needed another card of six
to develop further.

2712
02:03:11,797 --> 02:03:13,967
But the chances were really low.

2713
02:03:15,367 --> 02:03:17,467
You've discarded card six in green.

2714
02:03:18,677 --> 02:03:20,737
Nam Hee, it's your turn.

2715
02:03:20,737 --> 02:03:21,747
I'll take a back card.

2716
02:03:21,747 --> 02:03:23,647
The back card has been selected.

2717
02:03:25,247 --> 02:03:26,777
We've gone around twice, right?

2718
02:03:27,017 --> 02:03:28,787
- You've picked cards twice.
- I've picked twice, right?

2719
02:03:28,787 --> 02:03:30,287
(Front card: 6, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2720
02:03:33,117 --> 02:03:35,287
You've discarded card two in red.

2721
02:03:36,587 --> 02:03:39,557
The sum had to be higher than 17.

2722
02:03:39,557 --> 02:03:41,467
But I couldn't get the number.

2723
02:03:41,827 --> 02:03:44,027
It's your turn, Seung Yong.

2724
02:03:44,027 --> 02:03:45,037
I'll take a back card.

2725
02:03:45,037 --> 02:03:48,907
(Front card: 2, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2726
02:03:48,907 --> 02:03:51,877
(Front card: 4, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2727
02:03:53,177 --> 02:03:55,207
You've discarded card eight in yellow.

2728
02:03:55,207 --> 02:03:57,207
Actually, I got a good hand,

2729
02:03:57,207 --> 02:04:01,387
so my sum was way over 16.

2730
02:04:01,387 --> 02:04:04,887
But Sung Joo's sum wasn't over 16.

2731
02:04:04,887 --> 02:04:07,687
So I was waiting for the signal.

2732
02:04:09,187 --> 02:04:11,357
You Hyun, it's your turn.

2733
02:04:12,657 --> 02:04:13,657
I'll take a back card.

2734
02:04:13,957 --> 02:04:15,927
The back card has been selected.

2735
02:04:15,927 --> 02:04:17,497
(Front card: 8, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2736
02:04:17,497 --> 02:04:20,497
(Front card: 7, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2737
02:04:29,247 --> 02:04:31,447
You've discarded card seven in green.

2738
02:04:32,217 --> 02:04:35,517
Sung Joo discarded
a card in green beforehand.

2739
02:04:36,617 --> 02:04:38,687
You've discarded card six in green.

2740
02:04:39,287 --> 02:04:41,527
That means it isn't needed.

2741
02:04:41,527 --> 02:04:43,357
(He chose to discard a card in green
that Sung Joo doesn't need.)

2742
02:04:44,257 --> 02:04:46,627
Sung Joo, it's your turn.

2743
02:04:46,627 --> 02:04:48,697
(Front card: 7, You Hyun, Sung Joo,
Nam Hee, Seung Yong)

2744
02:04:48,697 --> 02:04:49,767
I'll take a back card.

2745
02:04:49,767 --> 02:04:51,637
