3146
02:24:09,957 --> 02:24:12,357
Kim You Hyun has lost all Lives.

3147
02:24:13,097 --> 02:24:15,727
Team Rookie wins Round One.

3148
02:24:15,797 --> 02:24:16,797
Good game!

3149
02:24:17,697 --> 02:24:19,267
Why didn't you take ten?

3150
02:24:19,297 --> 02:24:20,737
Since I was 15.

3151
02:24:20,737 --> 02:24:22,337
I also overlapped with red.

3152
02:24:22,337 --> 02:24:24,467
I wouldn't have done that
had I didn't overlap.

3153
02:24:24,467 --> 02:24:26,237
- So...
- But in the beginning...

3154
02:24:27,477 --> 02:24:31,107
I believe the time
to make the biggest move is Round One.

3155
02:24:31,107 --> 02:24:32,747
After securing an easy win in Round One,

3156
02:24:32,847 --> 02:24:35,077
when they have learned what to do
in Round Two,

3157
02:24:35,147 --> 02:24:37,487
I believe it's a chance
to go for a showdown.

3158
02:24:37,687 --> 02:24:40,217
I don't understand
losing Round One helplessly.

3159
02:24:40,557 --> 02:24:42,187
There wasn't any issue.

3160
02:24:42,187 --> 02:24:45,087
There was one mistake that You Hyun made.

3161
02:24:45,487 --> 02:24:47,397
If one gets discarded,

3162
02:24:47,397 --> 02:24:48,957
it's better for the same one
to lose another one.

3163
02:24:49,097 --> 02:24:51,567
The one who loses it
should become the tank.

3164
02:24:51,867 --> 02:24:54,837
Let's say that we lost one of our cubes...

3165
02:24:54,967 --> 02:24:57,407
and we're about to lose another one.

3166
02:24:57,737 --> 02:24:58,737
(Nam Hee lost 1 Life in Round 1.)

3167
02:24:58,737 --> 02:24:59,737
Go ahead.

3168
02:24:59,737 --> 02:25:00,977
You're going to sacrifice yourself.

3169
02:25:01,737 --> 02:25:03,947
Kim You Hyun,
please reveal your card combination.

3170
02:25:03,947 --> 02:25:06,617
(You Hyun purposely played a low number
to tank.)

3171
02:25:06,617 --> 02:25:08,317
If that happens,

3172
02:25:08,517 --> 02:25:10,787
the one who lost one Life,
must lose another.

3173
02:25:10,787 --> 02:25:13,717
It's good to make it 3 to 1 like that.
The reason for that...

3174
02:25:13,717 --> 02:25:15,417
is because when
there are two or fewer lives,

3175
02:25:15,417 --> 02:25:16,687
the one who rings the bell
will get eliminated right away...

3176
02:25:16,687 --> 02:25:17,727
if they fail to win.

3177
02:25:18,457 --> 02:25:19,857
The one with three Lives...

3178
02:25:19,857 --> 02:25:22,057
can still survive after ringing the bell.

3179
02:25:22,397 --> 02:25:23,597
- That's right.
- Right.

3180
02:25:23,697 --> 02:25:25,367
If you lose one, lose another.

3181
02:25:25,727 --> 02:25:27,397
Starting from Round Two,

3182
02:25:27,397 --> 02:25:29,137
we strategized with more detail.

3183
02:25:29,137 --> 02:25:30,437
The further we move into the rounds,

3184
02:25:30,867 --> 02:25:32,107
there could be massive numbers.

3185
02:25:32,107 --> 02:25:34,377
The opponents could set up traps as well.

3186
02:25:34,377 --> 02:25:36,177
We have to decide
if we are going to maintain 15...

3187
02:25:36,177 --> 02:25:37,847
or go for 14.

3188
02:25:38,307 --> 02:25:39,477
This is my suggestion.

3189
02:25:39,477 --> 02:25:42,117
You can decide if you want to
do this or not.

3190
02:25:42,177 --> 02:25:44,387
When we receive the first card,

3191
02:25:44,387 --> 02:25:47,087
if the number is around 12,

3192
02:25:47,087 --> 02:25:48,757
I don't think it will matter
if we decide to lose right away.

3193
02:25:48,787 --> 02:25:49,787
I think that will be okay.

3194
02:25:49,787 --> 02:25:50,827
- With 12?
- In the end...

3195
02:25:50,827 --> 02:25:52,227
Right. Around 12 or 13.

3196
02:25:52,327 --> 02:25:54,597
Do we go right away if it's over 12?

3197
02:25:54,597 --> 02:25:56,327
It will be 13, 14, or 15.

3198
02:25:56,327 --> 02:25:57,897
It's 13 just for Round 1.

3199
02:25:58,327 --> 02:25:59,967
- We'll maintain 14 after that.
- Right.

3200
02:25:59,967 --> 02:26:02,337
- We'll go with 15 at Round 4.
- Sounds good.

3201
02:26:02,337 --> 02:26:03,437
We can't give them a chance.

3202
02:26:03,437 --> 02:26:06,577
There are many instances when the flow
is given away and the tables get turned.

3203
02:26:06,577 --> 02:26:07,907
We have to kill them off when we can.

3204
02:26:08,037 --> 02:26:09,907
This is what we must do.

3205
02:26:10,177 --> 02:26:13,017
Let's say we have the same color
in Round One.

3206
02:26:13,317 --> 02:26:15,017
We can't have the same color.

3207
02:26:15,217 --> 02:26:16,747
We need a signal based on that.

3208
02:26:16,747 --> 02:26:18,817
You two should come up with one.
We'll come up with one as well.

3209
02:26:18,817 --> 02:26:22,287
Right. Anyway, we need a signal
based on that.

3210
02:26:22,787 --> 02:26:24,857
After Round One,

3211
02:26:24,857 --> 02:26:28,497
I felt the need to share this
with my teammates.

3212
02:26:28,497 --> 02:26:31,727
I suggested that
we keep signaling each other...

3213
02:26:31,727 --> 02:26:34,997
