03:07:38,227 --> 03:07:39,297
Goodness.

4191
03:07:39,297 --> 03:07:40,997
She says I have ten seconds left.

4192
03:07:40,997 --> 03:07:43,637
- Sorry.
- Ten seconds left.

4193
03:07:45,037 --> 03:07:47,707
Card seven in blue has been discarded.

4194
03:07:47,707 --> 03:07:48,707
(Gosh)

4195
03:07:48,707 --> 03:07:49,907
How high could it be?

4196
03:07:49,907 --> 03:07:51,377
It's Hyun Sung Joo's turn.

4197
03:07:51,977 --> 03:07:53,177
I'll take a front card.

4198
03:07:53,777 --> 03:07:57,277
Gosh, you fool. Why would you discard
a card seven in blue?

4199
03:07:57,777 --> 03:07:59,087
I'll take a front card.

4200
03:07:59,487 --> 03:08:04,817
(Sung Joo took a 4 in blue
on his previous turn.)

4201
03:08:04,817 --> 03:08:07,587
It's obvious
Sung Joon wants blue right now,

4202
03:08:07,857 --> 03:08:10,057
and he goes and discards a seven in blue.

4203
03:08:11,157 --> 03:08:15,637
He must have a plan.
I'm sure he has a brilliant plan.

4204
03:08:16,837 --> 03:08:18,197
His maximum has to be low.

4205
03:08:19,307 --> 03:08:20,867
(Kim You Hyun, Hyun Sung Joo,
Kim Kyoung Hoon, Shin Seung Yong)

4206
03:08:20,867 --> 03:08:22,737
I don't think it can be low,
since he took the seven in blue.

4207
03:08:23,507 --> 03:08:25,507
His maximum would be around 21 to 24.

4208
03:08:26,207 --> 03:08:28,447
Card four in blue has been discarded.

4209
03:08:28,447 --> 03:08:29,917
(Front card, Kim You Hyun, Hyun Sung Joo,
Kim Kyoung Hoon, Shin Seung Yong)

4210
03:08:29,917 --> 03:08:31,617
It's Kim Kyoung Hoon's turn.

4211
03:08:31,617 --> 03:08:32,687
I won't choose a card.

4212
03:08:32,987 --> 03:08:34,917
The back card has been selected.

4213
03:08:35,557 --> 03:08:36,617
(Card 9 in green)

4214
03:08:36,617 --> 03:08:38,827
Why must I suffer like this?

4215
03:08:42,697 --> 03:08:44,757
Card three in yellow has been discarded.

4216
03:08:45,397 --> 03:08:46,997
It's Shin Seung Yong's turn.

4217
03:08:46,997 --> 03:08:48,737
(Front card, Kim You Hyun, Hyun Sung Joo,
Kim Kyoung Hoon, Shin Seung Yong)

4218
03:08:48,737 --> 03:08:49,867
(Goodness)

4219
03:08:49,867 --> 03:08:52,967
I'm sorry, but could you tell me
how many back cards are left?

4220
03:08:54,107 --> 03:08:55,737
I think there's about six.

4221
03:08:55,737 --> 03:08:57,007
I'll take a front card.

4222
03:08:57,277 --> 03:08:59,747
Card three in yellow has been selected.

4223
03:08:59,747 --> 03:09:00,807
(Front card, Kim You Hyun, Hyun Sung Joo,
Kim Kyoung Hoon, Shin Seung Yong)

4224
03:09:00,807 --> 03:09:02,047
What do you think Seung Yong has?

4225
03:09:07,887 --> 03:09:10,217
Card two in red has been discarded.

4226
03:09:11,317 --> 03:09:12,927
It's Hyun Sung Joo's turn.

4227
03:09:14,657 --> 03:09:15,697
I'll discard this one.

4228
03:09:16,027 --> 03:09:17,797
Card two in red has been discarded.

4229
03:09:18,297 --> 03:09:20,627
- It's Kim Kyoung Hoon's turn.
- He's not giving away any information.

4230
03:09:22,667 --> 03:09:27,637
(The deck is slowly running out.)

4231
03:09:31,507 --> 03:09:32,847
It's Shin Seung Yong's turn.

4232
03:09:34,907 --> 03:09:37,017
I'll just end it. Let's end it.

4233
03:09:40,947 --> 03:09:41,947
I'll take the back card.

4234
03:09:42,287 --> 03:09:44,087
The back card has been selected.

4235
03:09:44,087 --> 03:09:47,657
(Seung Yong takes the final back card.)

4236
03:09:48,487 --> 03:09:50,757
Card one in yellow has been discarded.

4237
03:09:54,897 --> 03:09:56,697
I never felt like giving up
because of the score.

4238
03:09:57,237 --> 03:09:59,837
If we can just tie it up again,

4239
03:10:00,337 --> 03:10:01,707
we can regain momentum.

4240
03:10:02,107 --> 03:10:03,437
So my goal was to make it a tie first.

4241
03:10:03,737 --> 03:10:05,777
Kim You Hyun, please reveal your cards.

4242
03:10:05,777 --> 03:10:06,777
(Team C's Kim You Hyun's
card combination gets revealed.)

4243
03:10:06,777 --> 03:10:07,847
Mine's low too.

4244
03:10:09,477 --> 03:10:10,617
Mine's low too.

4245
03:10:10,877 --> 03:10:12,087
(Team C's Kim You Hyun's total: 20)

4246
03:10:12,087 --> 03:10:15,087
- Kim You Hyun's total is 20.
- That's too low.

4247
03:10:15,217 --> 03:10:16,457
- Yes.
- That's way too low.

4248
03:10:16,787 --> 03:10:19,027
- It's 20? Gosh.
- Hyun Sung Joo, please reveal your cards.

4249
03:10:19,257 --> 03:10:20,957
(Team R's Hyun Sung Joo's total: 21)

4250
03:10:20,957 --> 03:10:23,527
Hyun Sung Joo's total is 21.

4251
03:10:24,397 --> 03:10:26,627
Kim Kyoung Hoon, please reveal your cards.

4252
03:10:26,927 --> 03:10:29,167
Kim Kyoung Hoon's total is 31.

4253
03:10:29,567 --> 03:10:31,467
Shin Seung Yong, please reveal your cards.

4254
03:10:31,467 --> 03:10:33,867
(Team R's Shin Seung Yong's
card combination is revealed.)

4255
03:10:33,867 --> 03:10:36,907
(Team R's Shin Seung Yong's total: 3)

4256
03:10:36,907 --> 03:10:42,777
(Team R's Shin Seung Yong's total: 9)

4257
03:10:42,777 --> 03:10:44,277
(Team R's Shin Seung Yong's total: 17)

4258
03:10:44,277 --> 03:10:48,647
(Team R's Shin Seung Yong's total: 27)

4259
03:10:48,647 --> 03:10:49,757
Good game, everyone.

4260
03:10:49,757 --> 03:10:52,157
- Good game.
- Shin Seung Yong's total is 27.

4261
03:10:52,427 --> 03:10:55,157
Kim You Hyun's total is the lowest.

4262
03:10:55,157 --> 03:10:56,997
Please return one Life.

4263
03:10:56,997 --> 03:10:57,997
Good game.

4264
03:10:59,227 --> 03:11:02,437
(Team R wins Round 3.)

4265
03:11:02,437 --> 03:11:03,797
There it is.

4266
03:11:05,337 --> 03:11:08,407
We worked well together,
and, of course, we got lucky too.

4267
03:11:08,877 --> 03:11:11,277
Overall, it was a clean win.

4268
03:11:11,637 --> 03:11:12,847
Still, I think...

4269
03:11:12,847 --> 03:11:15,717
I played the biggest role in this game.

4270
03:11:15,877 --> 03:11:18,077
The Deathmatch is over.

4271
03:11:18,277 --> 03:11:21,117
All players,
please gather in the main hall.

4272
03:11:24,217 --> 03:11:26,927
The result of the Deathmatch
will be announced.

4273
03:11:27,587 --> 03:11:30,057
The team eliminated
from Bloody Game X is...

4274
03:11:32,327 --> 03:11:34,027
Team Challenger.

4275
03:11:34,567 --> 03:11:35,567
What?

4276
03:11:36,197 --> 03:11:37,597
- Seriously?
- Why?

4277
03:11:39,107 --> 03:11:41,967
How did Team Challenger lose?

4278
03:11:42,677 --> 03:11:44,877
They lost even with You Hyun
on their team?

4279
03:11:46,077 --> 03:11:49,017
- What?
- Were Beom and Seung Yong that good?

4280
03:11:49,177 --> 03:11:53,117
Did they have some hidden mental skills
that I didn't know about?

4281
03:11:53,117 --> 03:11:55,687
They were even outnumbered.

4282
03:11:57,157 --> 03:12:00,157
They're definitely not a team
to be underestimated.

4283
03:12:00,657 --> 03:12:02,727
How did Team C lose?

4284
03:12:04,097 --> 03:12:05,797
What kind of game did they play?

4285
03:12:05,827 --> 03:12:07,867
What on earth goes on at the Deathmatch?

4286
03:12:07,967 --> 03:12:09,897
The world of competition is unpredictable.

4287
03:12:10,897 --> 03:12:12,767
It's like when a weed refuses to die...

4288
03:12:12,767 --> 03:12:14,537
and somehow keeps hanging on.

4289
03:12:14,537 --> 03:12:15,737
That's actually the scariest.

4290
03:12:15,937 --> 03:12:19,077
Seung Yong's tenacity...

4291
03:12:19,077 --> 03:12:21,677
and strength are...

4292
03:12:22,447 --> 03:12:23,677
slowly...

4293
03:12:23,677 --> 03:12:25,717
starting to shine.

4294
03:12:25,717 --> 03:12:28,787
There's also Kwak Beom, who's great
at making split-second decisions.

4295
03:12:29,117 --> 03:12:31,387
Team R isn't an easy opponent.

4296
03:12:31,887 --> 03:12:35,257
All members of Team Challenger,
please pack your bags immediately...

4297
03:12:35,257 --> 03:12:37,627
and leave the Bloody Mansion.

4298
03:12:46,567 --> 03:12:48,337
- Good game.
- Good game.

4299
03:12:48,337 --> 03:12:50,107
- You did a great job.
- You did a great job.

4300
03:12:50,107 --> 03:12:51,137
I'll see you outside.

4301
03:12:51,877 --> 03:12:54,107
- Gosh, you did well.
- You too.

4302
03:12:54,107 --> 03:12:55,717
You did so well.

4303
03:12:56,117 --> 03:12:57,847
It's really such a shame.

4304
03:12:58,047 --> 03:13:01,987
As the oldest member of the team,

4305
03:13:01,987 --> 03:13:05,217
I naturally felt that
I had to protect them...

4306
03:13:05,217 --> 03:13:07,087
and take care of everyone.

4307
03:13:07,227 --> 03:13:08,927
Do you think you can handle it?

4308
03:13:09,397 --> 03:13:12,097
I think that thought stayed with me...

4309
03:13:12,227 --> 03:13:14,497
from the beginning to the very end.

4310
03:13:14,497 --> 03:13:17,567
I don't even know
whether I did a good job or not,

4311
03:13:18,037 --> 03:13:20,807
but it was quite a burden
and definitely stressful.

4312
03:13:20,867 --> 03:13:22,277
On the other hand,

4313
03:13:22,377 --> 03:13:24,907
the fact that Kyoung Hoon
and the rest of my team...

4314
03:13:24,907 --> 03:13:26,747
came together without even telling me...

4315
03:13:26,747 --> 03:13:29,077
and pooled all their funds to save me...

4316
03:13:29,547 --> 03:13:32,147
is something you rarely get to experience
in a survival show.

4317
03:13:32,247 --> 03:13:34,187
I was genuinely moved by that.

4318
03:13:34,287 --> 03:13:37,757
I already find myself
wanting to do this one more time.

4319
03:13:37,757 --> 03:13:40,757
I wonder if there's
something wrong with me...

4320
03:13:40,757 --> 03:13:42,187
for feeling that way.

4321
03:13:42,897 --> 03:13:44,157
Gosh.

4322
03:13:45,157 --> 03:13:47,327
Make sure you survive,
now that it's come to this.

4323
03:13:48,727 --> 03:13:50,537
- What?
- Gosh, I really thought...

4324
03:13:50,637 --> 03:13:51,867
I felt...

4325
03:13:52,567 --> 03:13:53,607
so disappointed.

4326
03:13:53,607 --> 03:13:55,237
I was so disappointed to
have to leave like this.

4327
03:13:55,237 --> 03:13:57,277
In my previous survival show,

4328
03:13:57,277 --> 03:13:59,647
I was unfortunately eliminated
way too early.

4329
03:13:59,747 --> 03:14:01,877
So this time,

4330
03:14:01,877 --> 03:14:03,477
I joined Bloody Game X...

4331
03:14:03,477 --> 03:14:06,847
with a determination to survive
as long as possible.

4332
03:14:08,787 --> 03:14:11,217
And I really loved my team.

4333
03:14:14,087 --> 03:14:15,187
Yes.

4334
03:14:20,997 --> 03:14:23,367
Actually,

4335
03:14:26,507 --> 03:14:29,177
the only reason I was able to make it
midway through the game...

4336
03:14:29,237 --> 03:14:32,037
is because of my team.
I'm so grateful for them.

4337
03:14:32,277 --> 03:14:33,547
This was...

4338
03:14:34,607 --> 03:14:36,817
a very happy experience for me.

4339
03:14:37,917 --> 03:14:39,447
- Well played, Kyoung Hoon.
- Good luck.

4340
03:14:40,687 --> 03:14:41,917
Great work.

4341
03:14:42,117 --> 03:14:43,687
Yes, well.

4342
03:14:44,617 --> 03:14:46,487
We became the second team
to be eliminated.

4343
03:14:46,887 --> 03:14:49,997
It had been ten years
since I appeared on "The Genius."

4344
03:14:50,257 --> 03:14:52,927
Back then, I was just
an immature graduate student,

4345
03:14:53,797 --> 03:14:55,737
and so much has changed since then.

4346
03:14:56,137 --> 03:14:57,867
I was so curious about...

4347
03:14:57,867 --> 03:15:00,667
how much I had improved,
which parts of me had grown,

4348
03:15:00,667 --> 03:15:03,437
and what parts of me had
actually gotten worse...

4349
03:15:03,437 --> 03:15:05,477
over these past ten years.

4350
03:15:05,577 --> 03:15:08,207
I joined this show
with that curiosity in mind.

4351
03:15:08,277 --> 03:15:10,417
I'm someone who enjoys betrayals.

4352
03:15:10,417 --> 03:15:11,877
I play just for fun.

4353
03:15:11,877 --> 03:15:13,717
If I become a Deathmatch candidate today,

4354
03:15:13,717 --> 03:15:14,987
can you make sure I survive
no matter what?

4355
03:15:15,287 --> 03:15:17,687
Just thinking
about those things gives me a thrill.

4356
03:15:18,217 --> 03:15:21,327
When I first did a survival show,
I was terrified.

4357
03:15:21,627 --> 03:15:24,197
I was scared and had no one to rely on.

4358
03:15:24,857 --> 03:15:26,227
Thinking that...

4359
03:15:26,527 --> 03:15:28,867
Ji Hoo must be feeling...

4360
03:15:28,867 --> 03:15:30,437
those same emotions...

4361
03:15:30,697 --> 03:15:32,567
made him seem kind of adorable.

4362
03:15:33,037 --> 03:15:36,577
And when I got here,
I started thinking about...

4363
03:15:36,577 --> 03:15:37,977
what it would have been like...

4364
03:15:37,977 --> 03:15:40,177
if there had been someone
who reached out to me back then...

4365
03:15:40,177 --> 03:15:42,917
and said, "Hey, we got this together."

4366
03:15:42,917 --> 03:15:44,317
I think that's why
I grew more attached to Ji Hoo.

4367
03:15:44,317 --> 03:15:45,617
I wanted to look out for him more.

4368
03:15:45,717 --> 03:15:48,847
Whenever we were trying to do something,
whether it was You Hyun or whoever,

4369
03:15:48,847 --> 03:15:50,617
I kept saying that...

4370
03:15:50,617 --> 03:15:53,157
we should give Ji Hoo a chance.

4371
03:15:54,027 --> 03:15:55,427
I think...

4372
03:15:56,197 --> 03:15:58,327
this was such a great experience...

4373
03:15:59,267 --> 03:16:02,367
where I got to look back on myself
while being...

4374
03:16:02,567 --> 03:16:03,897
completely immersed in the game.

4375
03:16:09,807 --> 03:16:11,107
Gosh, our youngest.

4376
03:16:11,207 --> 03:16:13,077
I can't believe you got eliminated.

4377
03:16:13,747 --> 03:16:15,607
Honestly, I was just dazed.

4378
03:16:15,607 --> 03:16:16,947
Am I really going home like this?

4379
03:16:16,947 --> 03:16:18,547
It didn't feel real.

4380
03:16:18,847 --> 03:16:20,587
I came here to win,

4381
03:16:22,687 --> 03:16:24,417
but I got eliminated way sooner
than I expected.

4382
03:16:24,587 --> 03:16:25,757
Well,

4383
03:16:25,757 --> 03:16:27,187
it wasn't because of bad luck.

4384
03:16:27,187 --> 03:16:29,997
It was purely my own lack of skill.

4385
03:16:30,527 --> 03:16:32,257
My team had complete faith in me
and supported me.

4386
03:16:32,257 --> 03:16:35,627
I was in the absolute ideal situation.

4387
03:16:35,627 --> 03:16:37,037
But even with all that,

4388
03:16:37,337 --> 03:16:38,897
I still got eliminated...

4389
03:16:39,907 --> 03:16:41,207
because I wasn't good enough.

4390
03:16:41,267 --> 03:16:42,737
It's all my fault,

4391
03:16:42,907 --> 03:16:46,107
and I feel incredibly sorry to my team,
Kyoung Hoon, You Hyun,

4392
03:16:46,477 --> 03:16:47,777
and Nam Hee.

4393
03:16:48,047 --> 03:16:49,517
- Thank you for everything.
- You did great.

4394
03:16:49,947 --> 03:16:51,547
- See you.
- Take care.

4395
03:16:51,977 --> 03:16:53,287
Thank you for everything.

4396
03:16:53,717 --> 03:16:56,057
You all worked so hard. Take care.

4397
03:16:57,287 --> 03:16:58,717
It was an honor.

4398
03:17:00,927 --> 03:17:02,427
What if they make us ambush again?

4399
03:17:02,427 --> 03:17:04,097
- No.
- Gosh, no.

4400
03:17:04,557 --> 03:17:05,767
You still want to do that?

4401
03:17:05,867 --> 03:17:07,027
I want to ambush too.

4402
03:17:07,267 --> 03:17:08,767
Ji Hoo, you really did great today.

4403
03:17:08,767 --> 03:17:10,897
Right, everyone did
such a great job today.

4404
03:17:10,897 --> 03:17:13,707
Yes. I really hoped that you would
get to finish what you started.

4405
03:17:13,867 --> 03:17:15,837
- I was...
- I wanted you to make it to the finals.

4406
03:17:16,507 --> 03:17:17,577
- Me too.
- What?

4407
03:17:17,577 --> 03:17:19,077
- I was strategizing too.
- Right.

4408
03:17:25,177 --> 03:17:26,887
- Especially You Hyun and Ji Hoo.
- Yes.

4409
03:17:27,047 --> 03:17:28,747
- I can't believe Team C was eliminated.
- Right.

4410
03:17:28,947 --> 03:17:30,817
Gosh. Great job, Team Rookie.

4411
03:17:30,817 --> 03:17:32,827
Congratulations.

4412
03:17:32,827 --> 03:17:35,127
- Come here.
- Rookie, Rookie.

4413
03:17:35,127 --> 03:17:36,757
- Congratulations.
- Rookie, Rookie.

4414
03:17:36,757 --> 03:17:38,127
- Goodness.
- Gosh.

4415
03:17:38,227 --> 03:17:39,367
- Gosh.
- Team Rookie.

4416
03:17:39,827 --> 03:17:40,867
You guys are insane.

4417
03:17:42,327 --> 03:17:45,037
Team Rookie defeated Team Challenger
like it was nothing.

4418
03:17:46,007 --> 03:17:49,137
They started out rough...

4419
03:17:49,137 --> 03:17:52,007
with quite a dramatic initiation.

4420
03:17:52,007 --> 03:17:53,577
But at some point,

4421
03:17:53,747 --> 03:17:56,077
they've begun turning into veterans.

4422
03:17:57,047 --> 03:17:58,317
Games like this...

4423
03:17:59,387 --> 03:18:00,917
There is an announcement.

4424
03:18:04,557 --> 03:18:06,287
As of tomorrow, all teams...

4425
03:18:07,157 --> 03:18:08,387
will be disbanded.

4426
03:18:08,927 --> 03:18:10,027
As of tomorrow?

4427
03:18:10,027 --> 03:18:12,327
With all teams disbanding
starting tomorrow,

4428
03:18:12,727 --> 03:18:15,167
the Money Challenge will become
an individual competition.

4429
03:18:15,167 --> 03:18:17,497
The final winner of Bloody Game X...

4430
03:18:18,397 --> 03:18:19,467
will be...

4431
03:18:19,467 --> 03:18:20,667
a single person.

4432
03:18:21,037 --> 03:18:24,337
Also, the outdoor survival grounds
will be closed.

4433
03:18:24,637 --> 03:18:27,607
Jin Ho and Seong Beom...

4434
03:18:27,607 --> 03:18:29,317
are not easy players...

4435
03:18:29,317 --> 03:18:31,277
to have as enemies.

4436
03:18:31,417 --> 03:18:32,787
Having a team...

4437
03:18:32,787 --> 03:18:35,987
and having to survive alone from now on...

4438
03:18:35,987 --> 03:18:38,217
feel completely different.

4439
03:18:38,357 --> 03:18:39,787
I have to switch my mindset.

4440
03:18:39,787 --> 03:18:40,987
I have to focus.

4441
03:18:41,087 --> 03:18:42,957
It's really disappointing...

4442
03:18:43,227 --> 03:18:45,967
because I felt like I was benefiting
from my team.

4443
03:18:46,327 --> 03:18:48,467
Even though
it's an individual competition now,

4444
03:18:48,467 --> 03:18:52,197
I think forming an alliance with
the members of Team P3 would be best.

4445
03:18:52,297 --> 03:18:53,407
I prefer an individual competition.

4446
03:18:54,437 --> 03:18:55,567
Relying on the human calculator...

4447
03:18:55,567 --> 03:18:56,707
and relying on someone else
to drive the bus...

4448
03:18:56,707 --> 03:18:57,877
are things that...

4449
03:18:57,877 --> 03:18:59,677
I'm getting a little tired of.

4450
03:18:59,777 --> 03:19:02,507
With teams, it's just the same group of
smart people doing the same things.

4451
03:19:02,507 --> 03:19:04,847
Being on that team
increases my chances of winning,

4452
03:19:04,847 --> 03:19:06,187
but it makes things way less exciting.

4453
03:19:06,447 --> 03:19:08,287
We've come this far into the show.

4454
03:19:08,287 --> 03:19:10,087
I can't keep riding on
someone else's coattails forever.

4455
03:19:10,957 --> 03:19:12,657
- Gosh.
- What's going on?

4456
03:19:14,227 --> 03:19:16,657
How about the three of us
share information...

4457
03:19:16,657 --> 03:19:18,157
Of course.

4458
03:19:18,327 --> 03:19:20,467
We're sleeping in the same place
tonight anyway, right?

4459
03:19:20,527 --> 03:19:21,997
- Yes.
- I think we'll have time to talk.

4460
03:19:23,297 --> 03:19:24,797
The other teams will
probably do the same, right?

4461
03:19:26,537 --> 03:19:27,637
It may officially be
an individual competition,

4462
03:19:27,637 --> 03:19:29,477
but if there's even a tiny opening
for an alliance,

4463
03:19:29,477 --> 03:19:31,037
Team P3...

4464
03:19:31,037 --> 03:19:32,437
will never split up.

4465
03:19:36,577 --> 03:19:38,077
I'm sure that...

4466
03:19:38,077 --> 03:19:41,447
alliances will form,
whether people realize it or not.

4467
03:19:42,017 --> 03:19:45,957
And in that sense, I can now
pick and choose the people...

4468
03:19:46,057 --> 03:19:47,257
I actually want to work with.

4469
03:19:47,427 --> 03:19:49,927
Since we've been eating
and drinking together every day,

4470
03:19:50,857 --> 03:19:52,557
I've strangely been getting along
with everyone.

4471
03:19:52,697 --> 03:19:54,497
Should I go hang out with the others?

4472
03:19:55,967 --> 03:19:57,237
Socialize a little?

4473
03:19:57,667 --> 03:19:58,767
Gosh, this is...

4474
03:19:58,767 --> 03:20:01,007
Yes, it's...

4475
03:20:04,077 --> 03:20:05,477
I kind of...

4476
03:20:08,677 --> 03:20:14,047
(Sung Joo heads over to Team P1's room.)

4477
03:20:14,047 --> 03:20:15,847
- Hello.
- Gosh, he's here.

4478
03:20:15,887 --> 03:20:17,017
Welcome.

4479
03:20:17,317 --> 03:20:18,987
Now that it's an individual competition,

4480
03:20:18,987 --> 03:20:22,827
the player in last place will probably
get to choose...

4481
03:20:23,257 --> 03:20:24,697
who goes to the Deathmatch.

4482
03:20:25,197 --> 03:20:28,797
If the last-place player is from
either Team P1 or Team P3,

4483
03:20:28,927 --> 03:20:30,397
the person will definitely
choose Seung Yong.

4484
03:20:31,110 --> 03:20:32,740
Since the Heist Day,

4485
03:20:32,740 --> 03:20:35,480
Seung Yong's reputation
has really taken a hit.

4486
03:20:35,750 --> 03:20:38,950
So teaming up with him...

4487
03:20:39,580 --> 03:20:41,390
might put be in a pretty bad spot.

4488
03:20:41,390 --> 03:20:42,720
It seems like he's become a target.

4489
03:20:42,820 --> 03:20:45,220
I haven't heard all the details yet,

4490
03:20:47,760 --> 03:20:48,830
but...

4491
03:20:49,030 --> 03:20:51,230
I wouldn't say he's one of
my top alliance choices.

4492
03:20:52,360 --> 03:20:54,170
I might not be confident
that I can succeed on my own,

4493
03:20:54,170 --> 03:20:56,530
but I'm even less confident
that I'll be the one to get eliminated.
